WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.628
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:02.898 --> 00:04.642
[Direct Superior Officers] [Lieutenant Colonel Byeon Hyeok Jin]

3
00:04.642 --> 00:08.064
Wow, "Lieutenant Colonel Byeon Hyeok Jin."

4
00:08.064 --> 00:10.229
The name itself is savage.

5
00:10.229 --> 00:12.653
Hey! Line it up properly!

6
00:12.653 --> 00:14.664
What will the colonel say if he sees it?

7
00:14.664 --> 00:17.436
- Yes, okay. - Wow, this guy, seriously...

8
00:18.358 --> 00:19.783
Never in my entire service

9
00:19.783 --> 00:21.788
[Battalion Commander] have I seen congratulatory flowers.

10
00:21.788 --> 00:23.049
[Lieutenant Colonel Byeon Hyeok Jin]

11
00:23.049 --> 00:25.096
- Chungseong! Love you! - Chungseong! Love you!

12
00:25.096 --> 00:27.313
Yeah, love you too. Well done.

13
00:27.313 --> 00:28.899
- Thank you, sir! - Yeah.

14
00:32.258 --> 00:34.168
[Congratulations on your inauguration!]

15
00:34.168 --> 00:35.953
[Congratulations]

16
00:35.953 --> 00:37.246
[Congratulations, Lieutenant!]

17
00:39.496 --> 00:41.304
How'd they know about the Second Company patrol's rotation

18
00:41.304 --> 00:42.946
to get here to put all of this up?

19
00:42.946 --> 00:45.110
The commander's popularity's no joke.

20
00:45.110 --> 00:47.913
Yeah, he even missed the inauguration ceremony.

21
00:47.913 --> 00:49.486
This is what his message read.

22
00:49.486 --> 00:52.855
Thank you to all of you who congratulated me on my inauguration.

23
00:52.855 --> 00:56.240
However, I have to respectfully turn down the wreaths and flowers.

24
00:56.240 --> 00:59.061
If you would really like to, please send rice instead.

25
00:59.061 --> 01:01.278
This way we can share it with people in need.

26
01:01.278 --> 01:02.880
Goodness.

27
01:02.880 --> 01:06.067
I'm not certain, but I've heard this guy's a kid.

28
01:07.111 --> 01:09.831
[From the 6th Corps Commander...] Wow, even the corps commander sent stuff.

29
01:09.831 --> 01:11.591
[Song Jae Gwang] Oh, this guy's connections...

30
01:11.591 --> 01:13.944
He's really different from you.

31
01:15.270 --> 01:17.129
I never told you this, but...

32
01:17.129 --> 01:19.618
I've got some serious connections, too.

33
01:19.618 --> 01:21.281
Oh, really?

34
01:21.281 --> 01:23.961
Don't say internet connection or something like that.

35
01:23.961 --> 01:25.304
Huh?

36
01:25.304 --> 01:26.610
- Huh? - What?

37
01:26.610 --> 01:28.211
What?

38
01:30.598 --> 01:33.051
Hey, you joke too much!

39
01:33.051 --> 01:34.669
Ah, this guy, seriously.

40
01:34.669 --> 01:38.620
If I make battalion commander in the future, I'll send you one.

41
01:38.620 --> 01:41.675
Oh my, thank you for even saying that.

42
01:41.675 --> 01:44.785
But who knows if that day will ever come.

43
01:46.203 --> 01:48.974
Hey, of course it will!

44
01:48.974 --> 01:50.622
Oi, No Hee Jeong, did you order the guys to clean?

45
01:50.622 --> 01:51.661
Yes, I did.

46
01:51.661 --> 01:53.505
- Choi Il Gu. - Yes, sir?

47
01:53.505 --> 01:55.073
Did you update the situation board?

48
01:55.073 --> 01:58.328
Uh, no... Why would I...

49
01:58.328 --> 01:59.442
Hey, Choi Il Gu.

50
01:59.442 --> 02:01.510
- Yes, sir, I'm Choi... - Enough.

51
02:01.510 --> 02:04.796
You're an officer now. Start acting like one.

52
02:04.796 --> 02:06.118
Okay, I will, sir.

53
02:06.118 --> 02:07.197
What the hell is this?

54
02:07.197 --> 02:09.673
This just appeared now, I don't...

55
02:09.673 --> 02:11.775
For God's sake.

56
02:11.775 --> 02:13.155
Chungseong! Love you!

57
02:13.155 --> 02:15.088
Love you too! Where's the company commander?

58
02:15.088 --> 02:16.312
He should be here soon.

59
02:16.312 --> 02:17.691
Are you all waiting?

60
02:17.691 --> 02:19.235
That's right, he...

61
02:19.235 --> 02:20.849
told us all to wait in the barracks.

62
02:20.849 --> 02:21.850
Oh, I see, well done.

63
02:21.850 --> 02:23.929
One of you is missing?

64
02:25.275 --> 02:26.966
The platoon leader said

65
02:26.966 --> 02:30.272
he'd go ahead to receive the battalion commander.

66
02:30.272 --> 02:31.872
[Devotion to the Nation]

67
02:32.594 --> 02:34.071
Chungseong! Love you!

68
02:34.071 --> 02:36.114
Chungseong! Love you! You're doing great.

69
02:36.114 --> 02:37.745
Have a good day, sir!

70
02:43.294 --> 02:44.661
First Lieutenant Oh Seok Jin!

71
02:44.661 --> 02:47.695
Always combat-ready and prepared to respond to enemy prov...

72
02:47.695 --> 02:48.764
Is that too much?

73
02:48.764 --> 02:50.918
Oh, he's going to go places.

74
02:50.918 --> 02:53.089
Yeah, looks like he'll make captain in no time.

75
02:53.089 --> 02:54.423
So many bats in this unit.

76
02:54.423 --> 02:56.231
Corporal No Bat...

77
02:57.604 --> 02:59.663
- What? - Never mind.

78
02:59.663 --> 03:01.009
Okay, back to it then.

79
03:01.009 --> 03:02.337
Yes, sir.

80
03:08.488 --> 03:11.817
- You just flipped me off, didn't you? - Sorry? No!

81
03:11.817 --> 03:12.896
Yeah, you did.

82
03:12.896 --> 03:14.616
No, I didn't, I would never!

83
03:14.616 --> 03:15.738
You did so!

84
03:15.738 --> 03:17.605
No, sir, really, my glasses were slipping.

85
03:17.605 --> 03:19.047
I just used my index finger.

86
03:19.047 --> 03:22.160
If you get caught flipping someone off, you have to hang upside down and work.

87
03:22.160 --> 03:24.026
You have to eat upside down, too.

88
03:24.026 --> 03:26.223
And when you're sleeping.

89
03:26.223 --> 03:28.275
Corporal No Bat, understood, sir...

90
03:28.275 --> 03:31.520
Yoon Mo, pass me the scissors. Let's cut this bat off, come on!

91
03:31.520 --> 03:33.150
- Hey, Il Gu, call the medic! - No, I'm serious!

92
03:33.150 --> 03:34.533
- Ah, yes, okay! - It was an accident!

93
03:34.533 --> 03:35.635
I was just pushing them up, I swear!

94
03:35.635 --> 03:37.270
- Breathe, breathe! - No, no!

95
03:37.270 --> 03:39.308
It'll grow back, don't worry.

96
03:41.103 --> 03:43.544
It's boiling, right?

97
03:43.544 --> 03:45.486
When will the damn military get an air conditioner?

98
03:45.486 --> 03:46.770
What is this, a sci-fi movie?

99
03:46.770 --> 03:48.720
That'll never freaking happen.

100
03:48.720 --> 03:51.310
Still, getting to skip the inauguration was pretty sweet.

101
03:51.310 --> 03:54.691
I'm dying just thinking about standing around in that heat.

102
03:54.691 --> 03:57.558
I've heard he's pretty young. Maybe that's why he's a bit different.

103
03:57.558 --> 03:58.861
"Different," my ass.

104
03:58.861 --> 04:00.245
You know why he skipped inauguration?

105
04:00.245 --> 04:01.903
No, why did he?

106
04:01.903 --> 04:03.944
The last battalion commander got ousted that way.

107
04:03.944 --> 04:05.071
So would you do it if you were him?

108
04:05.071 --> 04:06.565
- Ah. - Jeon Se Gye!

109
04:06.565 --> 04:09.698
These folks are busy, but give them an autograph.

110
04:09.698 --> 04:13.056
You exploited Jeon Se Gye's sick mother and used an officer for personal gain.

111
04:13.056 --> 04:14.950
Can you still call yourself an officer?

112
04:14.950 --> 04:17.139
Is this what the military is?

113
04:18.835 --> 04:20.446
Hey, Jeon Sekai.

114
04:20.446 --> 04:21.810
Private Jeon Sekai!

115
04:21.810 --> 04:24.325
Do you know what happened to him?

116
04:24.325 --> 04:28.442
I also heard he was transferred somewhere, but I don't really know the details.

117
04:28.442 --> 04:30.218
I heard he went to the hospital to see his mom.

118
04:30.218 --> 04:33.240
Damn, he really put on a big show to get a lighter punishment.

119
04:33.240 --> 04:35.996
That blue blood was off from the get-go.

120
04:36.941 --> 04:39.424
Se Gye, how's your mother doing?

121
04:39.424 --> 04:42.158
When I saw her during leave, she was doing much better.

122
04:42.158 --> 04:43.851
I spent most of my time there.

123
04:43.851 --> 04:47.368
The hospital must've been chaos, huh?

124
04:47.368 --> 04:48.822
A little.

125
04:51.057 --> 04:53.625
I asked the nurses to take care of my mom.

126
04:53.625 --> 04:55.706
I took some pictures and signed some autographs, too.

127
04:55.706 --> 04:58.493
Hm, nothing else?

128
04:58.493 --> 05:02.150
They asked to send letters, so I gave them your names.

129
05:03.265 --> 05:05.474
Honestly, how could I not love you?

130
05:05.474 --> 05:06.637
Se Gye.

131
05:06.637 --> 05:08.576
Did you mention I'm getting discharged soon?

132
05:08.576 --> 05:10.156
I even told them your discharge date!

133
05:10.156 --> 05:11.763
- Yes! - Nice!

134
05:11.763 --> 05:14.464
Hey, Sergeant Choi, don't you have a girlfriend?

135
05:14.464 --> 05:16.198
Man, you're doing too much!

136
05:16.198 --> 05:18.073
Byeong Nam, don't forget Su Ah promised she'd arrange

137
05:18.073 --> 05:19.558
a group blind date for us when we're on leave!

138
05:19.558 --> 05:21.792
Don't worry about that, okay?

139
05:21.792 --> 05:23.480
My Su Ah is a beauty, remember?

140
05:23.480 --> 05:25.854
Pretty girls hang with pretty girls, birds of a feather, right?

141
05:25.854 --> 05:27.732
That's why beauty is pain!

142
05:27.732 --> 05:29.665
What are you on about...

143
05:43.760 --> 05:46.681
Chungseong! Love you!

144
05:50.453 --> 05:52.350
And with the rice out front,

145
05:52.350 --> 05:54.196
he said to gather it and donate it around the area,

146
05:54.196 --> 05:56.250
so once you're done, just stack them neatly to one side, okay?

147
05:56.250 --> 05:58.392
- Yes, sir. Go check. - Okay.

148
06:01.946 --> 06:03.867
The battalion commander is here.

149
06:07.928 --> 06:10.550
[Congratulations on your inauguration!]

150
06:26.219 --> 06:28.597
[EP02. Battalion Commander Byeon Hyeok Jin] Attention!

151
06:28.597 --> 06:30.004
Chungseong!

152
06:30.004 --> 06:31.381
Chungseong.

153
06:32.172 --> 06:33.978
- At ease. - At ease.

154
06:37.301 --> 06:39.283
Second Company Commander, Cho Baek Ho!

155
06:39.283 --> 06:41.258
Great, nice to meet you.

156
06:42.111 --> 06:44.157
First Sergeant, Park Jae Su!

157
06:44.157 --> 06:46.068
- First Sergeant, let's get along well. - Yes?

158
06:46.068 --> 06:47.668
Yes, sir.

159
06:48.585 --> 06:50.515
Assistant Platoon Leader, Sergeant Im Seong Min!

160
06:50.515 --> 06:52.204
Yes, nice to meet you.

161
06:53.080 --> 06:56.391
Senior Squad Leader, Staff Sergeant Choi Il Gu!

162
06:56.391 --> 06:57.938
I love your energy.

163
06:57.938 --> 06:59.649
Thank you, sir!

164
07:01.321 --> 07:04.148
Platoon Leader, First Lieutenant Oh Seok Jin!

165
07:04.148 --> 07:06.335
- First Lieutenant Oh Seok Jin. - Yes, sir!

166
07:06.335 --> 07:08.415
Look out for me, yeah?

167
07:09.076 --> 07:11.015
I'll look out for you, sir!

168
07:11.994 --> 07:13.594
Great.

169
07:15.004 --> 07:16.398
Hey, he just went into the admin office!

170
07:16.398 --> 07:18.347
- You're all ready, right? - Yes, sir!

171
07:18.347 --> 07:20.258
Okay, your nails are all cut?

172
07:20.258 --> 07:22.009
- Yes, they're cut! - Yes, sir!

173
07:22.009 --> 07:23.774
Okay.

174
07:23.774 --> 07:25.962
I saw him at the main entrance yesterday,

175
07:25.962 --> 07:27.722
and it was only for a second.

176
07:27.722 --> 07:29.367
But he was super intense.

177
07:29.367 --> 07:31.077
- Really? - Yeah.

178
07:31.077 --> 07:32.727
We're screwed.

179
07:32.727 --> 07:34.677
- Hey, Bit Na Ri. - Private First Class Moon Bit Na Ri!

180
07:34.677 --> 07:36.213
Don't mess up.

181
07:36.213 --> 07:37.915
- Understood, sir! - Okay.

182
07:37.915 --> 07:39.847
- Hey, new recruit. - Private Kim Hyeon Uk!

183
07:39.847 --> 07:42.308
- You have to do well. - I will, sir!

184
07:42.308 --> 07:44.657
Well, you'll do fine regardless.

185
07:44.657 --> 07:46.078
Thank you.

186
07:46.947 --> 07:48.738
Right, it's great to meet you all.

187
07:48.738 --> 07:50.560
I am Lieutenant Colonel Byeon Hyeok Jin.

188
07:50.560 --> 07:53.848
"Chungseong! Love you" is the Second Company's motto, right?

189
07:53.848 --> 07:54.933
Yes, that's correct!

190
07:54.933 --> 07:57.540
Right, "Love you."

191
07:58.297 --> 07:59.714
Well, it's good.

192
07:59.714 --> 08:02.739
- Let's get along well! - Yes, sir!

193
08:02.739 --> 08:06.127
I'd like to introduce myself to all the Second Company personnel, but...

194
08:06.127 --> 08:08.655
Ah, yes, I'll...

195
08:08.655 --> 08:10.824
You can do it h-here!

196
08:11.500 --> 08:14.378
- Thanks. - Corporal No Hee Jeong, thank you!

197
08:21.947 --> 08:24.120
Chungseong! Love you.

198
08:24.120 --> 08:28.468
I'm Lieutenant Colonel Byeon Hyeok Jin, the newly appointed Battalion Commander.

199
08:28.468 --> 08:30.151
I'll keep this brief.

200
08:30.151 --> 08:32.750
Bullshit. I'll call Dong Woo "hyung" if this is short.

201
08:32.750 --> 08:34.383
Oh, you promise?

202
08:34.383 --> 08:35.613
In the military,

203
08:35.613 --> 08:37.820
your time spent here is in no way a waste,

204
08:37.820 --> 08:40.325
nor is it a pause in your lives.

205
08:40.325 --> 08:43.090
To help you all change and grow,

206
08:43.090 --> 08:45.637
this unit will continue to transform alongside you

207
08:45.637 --> 08:47.736
to stoke that growth.

208
08:47.736 --> 08:49.064
That's all.

209
08:50.536 --> 08:51.557
"That's all?"

210
08:51.557 --> 08:53.767
Can it really be that short?

211
08:53.767 --> 08:54.887
What, why?

212
08:54.887 --> 08:57.420
Didn't you say you'd call me "hyung?"

213
08:57.420 --> 08:59.210
Are you crazy? You wanna die?

214
08:59.210 --> 09:01.536
- Wow! - Smooth.

215
09:01.536 --> 09:02.538
Did he really finish?

216
09:02.538 --> 09:04.360
In my entire military career,

217
09:04.360 --> 09:07.645
I've never heard an officer make a speech that short.

218
09:07.645 --> 09:09.022
- Do I just press this? - Oh, I'll...

219
09:09.022 --> 09:10.267
No, no, it's fine.

220
09:10.267 --> 09:11.857
Okay, sir...

221
09:11.857 --> 09:13.421
- Let's head to the barracks. - Yes, sir.

222
09:13.421 --> 09:14.965
I'll...

223
09:15.617 --> 09:17.016
Allow me to show you.

224
09:17.016 --> 09:18.020
First Lieutenant Oh Seok Jin.

225
09:18.020 --> 09:19.660
First Lieutenant Oh Seok Jin!

226
09:19.660 --> 09:21.215
No need to swarm us.

227
09:21.215 --> 09:24.570
The company commander and I will go by ourselves.

228
09:30.445 --> 09:31.959
I was just worried the commander was tired...

229
09:31.959 --> 09:33.248
Yes, of course.

230
09:33.248 --> 09:35.056
- Okay, back to it. - Yes, sir.

231
09:35.056 --> 09:36.550
By the way.

232
09:36.550 --> 09:39.638
Doesn't the new battalion commander seem pretty awesome?

233
09:39.638 --> 09:40.836
"In the military,

234
09:40.836 --> 09:43.919
your time spent here is in no way a waste nor is it a pause in your lives."

235
09:43.919 --> 09:45.627
When he was making that speech,

236
09:45.627 --> 09:47.397
he became my new role model.

237
09:47.397 --> 09:50.154
You have so many role models. It must be nice.

238
09:50.154 --> 09:52.005
Every damn person he sees becomes his "role model".

239
09:52.005 --> 09:54.664
But when I met you, it wasn't...

240
09:54.664 --> 09:55.870
What did you just say?

241
09:55.870 --> 09:58.588
- Nothing... - Hand me those scissors from earlier.

242
09:58.588 --> 10:00.361
- Yes, sir. - Come over here a second.

243
10:00.361 --> 10:02.851
I've got somewhere to be, so I'll just...

244
10:02.851 --> 10:04.656
Have a good day!

245
10:06.078 --> 10:07.624
He got good at reading the room, huh?

246
10:07.624 --> 10:08.785
Seems like it, sir.

247
10:08.785 --> 10:10.736
Unit, attention!

248
10:11.643 --> 10:13.897
Chungseong! Love you!

249
10:15.603 --> 10:17.784
- At ease. - At ease.

250
10:30.839 --> 10:32.800
Are you the newest recruit of the Second Company?

251
10:32.800 --> 10:34.246
Private Kim Hyeon Uk!

252
10:34.246 --> 10:35.754
Yes, that's correct!

253
10:35.754 --> 10:37.385
Well...

254
10:37.385 --> 10:39.639
I'm the greenest guy here now.

255
10:39.639 --> 10:40.900
Let's get along well!

256
10:40.900 --> 10:42.331
Private Kim Hyeon Uk!

257
10:42.331 --> 10:43.556
I'll work hard!

258
10:43.556 --> 10:46.063
Great, you're lively.

259
10:46.734 --> 10:48.083
Corporal Park Min Seok.

260
10:48.083 --> 10:50.453
Corporal Park Min Seok!

261
10:55.351 --> 10:57.241
Corporal Park Min Seok! Thank you!

262
10:57.241 --> 10:58.360
Nice to meet you.

263
10:58.360 --> 11:01.466
Ah, yes, nice to meet you, thank you!

264
11:01.466 --> 11:04.622
Ever since I heard Major General Park Chun Gyu's speech when I was a cadet,

265
11:04.622 --> 11:07.625
his words have really stayed with me.

266
11:07.625 --> 11:10.838
I have no doubt that under such a fine father,

267
11:10.838 --> 11:14.081
you'll serve as a fine soldier yourself.

268
11:14.081 --> 11:17.014
Yes, sir, I'll work hard!

269
11:17.014 --> 11:18.406
Great.

270
11:20.786 --> 11:24.354
Let's work well together, everyone!

271
11:24.354 --> 11:26.060
- Yes, sir! - Yes, sir!

272
11:26.060 --> 11:27.088
That's it.

273
11:27.088 --> 11:29.066
Unit, attention!

274
11:29.066 --> 11:31.616
Chungseong! Love you!

275
11:31.616 --> 11:33.652
Chungseong! Love you.

276
11:39.478 --> 11:41.628
He's way nicer than I thought?

277
11:41.628 --> 11:43.881
That's the first time I've seen someone like that.

278
11:43.881 --> 11:46.447
Yeah, he's not giving soldier energy.

279
11:46.447 --> 11:48.498
More like a team leader at a corporate company.

280
11:48.498 --> 11:50.564
He's actually so cool.

281
11:50.564 --> 11:52.976
It must be nice. Park Min Seok.

282
11:52.976 --> 11:55.022
Oh, Bbak Min Seok!

283
11:55.022 --> 11:57.594
Having a military dad really is the ultimate military cheat code.

284
11:57.594 --> 11:59.073
No way.

285
11:59.073 --> 12:01.325
What do you mean "no way," dude?

286
12:01.325 --> 12:03.689
You're definitely scoring a leave pass before you discharge.

287
12:03.689 --> 12:06.227
No, trust me, that's definitely not happening.

288
12:06.227 --> 12:09.254
That's exactly how the army works, dude.

289
12:09.254 --> 12:10.891
Full of energy, Second Company.

290
12:10.891 --> 12:12.674
Thank you.

291
12:12.674 --> 12:15.665
Effective tomorrow, this battalion's going to have some big changes.

292
12:15.665 --> 12:17.191
I'll be relying on you a lot, Commander Cho.

293
12:17.191 --> 12:18.748
Understood, sir.

294
12:18.748 --> 12:20.747
Wait, no.

295
12:20.747 --> 12:23.724
I should be the one making a good impression on you, Commander Cho.

296
12:23.724 --> 12:25.411
If I don't want to get booted.

297
12:27.966 --> 12:29.708
Ah, that's, I...

298
12:29.708 --> 12:31.382
I'm joking.

299
12:32.156 --> 12:34.351
Is that the next one?

300
12:34.351 --> 12:36.071
Yes, that's right.

301
12:40.372 --> 12:43.540
Hey, today's going to be brutal, so everyone stay safe out there.

302
12:43.540 --> 12:46.114
Hey, pick up the damn pace! Day's gonna be over by the time you get here!

303
12:46.114 --> 12:47.418
Yes, okay, sir!

304
12:47.418 --> 12:48.850
Quickly, run!

305
12:48.850 --> 12:51.278
Hey! Watch the sickles!

306
12:51.278 --> 12:53.029
Hey, hurry up, quickly!

307
12:53.822 --> 12:55.343
Final years, not running?

308
12:55.343 --> 12:58.569
I learned this pace back when you were a final year, Sergeant Choi!

309
12:58.569 --> 13:00.753
Cut us some slack!

310
13:00.753 --> 13:02.669
Shut up and hurry!

311
13:03.366 --> 13:04.492
Chungseong! Love you!

312
13:04.492 --> 13:05.798
What sort of salute is that?

313
13:05.798 --> 13:07.793
We're going to up and do some weeding.

314
13:07.793 --> 13:11.291
You boys holding sickles, stop messing around before you split someone's skull open.

315
13:11.291 --> 13:13.830
I'll explain more when we're there, come on.

316
13:13.830 --> 13:15.057
- Understood, sir! - Understood, sir!

317
13:15.057 --> 13:17.363
- Let's go up. - Yes, okay!

318
13:17.363 --> 13:19.725
Wow, the weeds have gotten pretty thick.

319
13:19.725 --> 13:20.922
Fertile soil there.

320
13:20.922 --> 13:23.563
Nearing discharge means we won't have to climb up here much more.

321
13:23.563 --> 13:25.103
The clouds are pretty!

322
13:25.103 --> 13:27.500
- Hey, everyone listen up. - Listening.

323
13:27.500 --> 13:29.242
We're gonna do some weeding now.

324
13:29.242 --> 13:31.485
First, clear out all of this side.

325
13:31.485 --> 13:33.460
Then we move over there.

326
13:33.460 --> 13:34.584
But if you look closely,

327
13:34.584 --> 13:37.514
that's the Command Sergeant Major's crop patch he manages.

328
13:37.514 --> 13:39.976
Only pull the weeds around it out.

329
13:39.976 --> 13:42.644
Mess anything up and you're going straight to the brig. I'm serious.

330
13:42.644 --> 13:43.749
You get what I'm saying?

331
13:43.749 --> 13:45.415
- Yes, understood. - Yes, understood.

332
13:45.415 --> 13:47.414
Okay, also...

333
13:47.414 --> 13:50.682
I hate looking at this thing, who's taking the weed-whacker?

334
13:50.682 --> 13:52.003
"Weed-whacker?"

335
13:52.003 --> 13:53.146
Is something wrong?

336
13:53.146 --> 13:54.529
Yeah, there is.

337
13:54.529 --> 13:57.671
Back in the day, it wasn't just used for weeds.

338
13:57.671 --> 13:59.875
Those were the fucking savage ages...

339
13:59.875 --> 14:01.372
Well, anyway.

340
14:01.372 --> 14:04.903
Weed-whacker volunteers, hands up!

341
14:07.056 --> 14:08.656
I don't want to.

342
14:10.314 --> 14:12.086
Look, it sucks, but someone has to do it.

343
14:12.086 --> 14:13.525
Shut your mouth, for God's...

344
14:13.525 --> 14:15.712
Hey, look here, I'll sweet-talk them.

345
14:15.712 --> 14:17.122
Try it.

346
14:17.122 --> 14:18.652
Uh... You.

347
14:18.652 --> 14:21.321
Look, anyone below Ji Jeong Min, gather around.

348
14:21.981 --> 14:23.667
Pass me that sickle.

349
14:23.667 --> 14:25.322
- Corporal Park Min Seok. - Okay.

350
14:25.322 --> 14:27.588
You guys think it'll be easier swinging this around?

351
14:27.588 --> 14:29.921
No way. Look at it, yeah?

352
14:29.921 --> 14:33.039
The blade's not even sharp. What can you even do?

353
14:33.039 --> 14:34.546
Scratch your back with it?

354
14:34.546 --> 14:37.623
Honestly, pulling them out by hand would be faster.

355
14:37.623 --> 14:41.024
- Bullshit. - For God's sake, what are you snickering at?

356
14:41.024 --> 14:43.197
You think doing it by hand will be easy?

357
14:43.197 --> 14:45.010
No way, try taking your gloves off later.

358
14:45.010 --> 14:46.996
Your fingers will all be green.

359
14:46.996 --> 14:50.079
You go on leave with hands like that and your mom will cry.

360
14:50.079 --> 14:53.426
You guys want to be terrible sons, huh?

361
14:54.850 --> 14:56.730
What's with this punk?

362
14:56.730 --> 14:58.555
Sorry, sir!

363
14:58.555 --> 15:00.240
But!

364
15:01.159 --> 15:02.811
Look at this weed-whacker.

365
15:02.811 --> 15:05.646
Just strap the engine on your back and walk straight.

366
15:05.646 --> 15:07.226
Fucking cake walk, right?

367
15:07.226 --> 15:08.367
Bullshit.

368
15:08.367 --> 15:11.705
Right, weed-whacker volunteers, hands up!

369
15:18.293 --> 15:19.746
Ah, these bastards.

370
15:19.746 --> 15:22.108
I really wasn't going to say this, but...

371
15:22.108 --> 15:24.924
You all know Sergeant Shim Jin Woo, right?

372
15:24.924 --> 15:26.935
- You know how to use a saw? - Yes, before the military, my nickname was...

373
15:26.935 --> 15:29.761
That guy used the weed-whacker so well that he made the First Sergeant's day.

374
15:29.761 --> 15:32.193
He got excused from tactical training to do it!

375
15:32.193 --> 15:35.218
I'm telling you, it's freaking gold!

376
15:37.145 --> 15:39.011
Of course, straight lies.

377
15:39.011 --> 15:41.166
Right, I'm really asking for the last time.

378
15:41.166 --> 15:43.853
Weed-whacker volunteers, hands up!

379
15:45.903 --> 15:48.375
Even a stray dog knows weed-whackers are brutal.

380
15:48.375 --> 15:49.658
Who the hell would do it?

381
15:49.658 --> 15:51.595
It's so freaking hot, please just do rock-paper-scissors.

382
15:51.595 --> 15:53.058
I'll start with you, Choi Byeong Nam, I swear.

383
15:53.058 --> 15:55.230
- Oh please, stop that. - Please, stop that.

384
15:55.230 --> 15:57.716
- Private Moon Bit Na Ri! - Ah, Jesus!

385
15:57.716 --> 15:59.334
I'll do it!

386
16:00.945 --> 16:04.149
Uh, anyone else? Nobody?

387
16:04.149 --> 16:05.904
There must be...

388
16:05.904 --> 16:08.128
There has to be, there must be!

389
16:08.128 --> 16:09.787
Private Moon Bit Na Ri!

390
16:09.787 --> 16:11.583
I've actually been waiting to do this.

391
16:11.583 --> 16:12.756
Really?

392
16:12.756 --> 16:14.557
Fine, okay, you do it.

393
16:14.557 --> 16:16.267
Thank you!

394
16:16.267 --> 16:18.228
- Ah... - I've got a bad feeling...

395
16:18.228 --> 16:20.044
He'll slice the whole unit up instead of the weeds.

396
16:20.044 --> 16:21.807
Hey, will you be okay?

397
16:21.807 --> 16:23.725
- I will! - Be careful.

398
16:23.725 --> 16:26.286
Shouldn't somebody stop him?

399
16:34.808 --> 16:37.481
Sergeant Choi, look, I have goosebumps!

400
16:37.481 --> 16:38.852
He cranked it up on the first pull...

401
16:38.852 --> 16:40.881
Is he a weed-whacking prodigy chosen by the Gods?

402
16:40.881 --> 16:43.326
There's no way it can start from the first pull!

403
16:43.326 --> 16:45.159
When it doesn't start up the first time in the blazing heat,

404
16:45.159 --> 16:48.012
it makes you want to smash the damn thing!

405
16:53.820 --> 16:55.992
You look so cool!

406
16:55.992 --> 16:57.422
Na Ri, you're awesome!

407
16:57.422 --> 16:59.343
- Yeah, so cool! - You're awesome!

408
16:59.343 --> 17:01.270
You look like Firebat!

409
17:01.270 --> 17:02.851
Hey, everyone back up!

410
17:02.851 --> 17:05.524
Hey, Bit Na Ri, go all the way to the end.

411
17:05.524 --> 17:07.071
- Yes, sir! - Okay.

412
17:10.245 --> 17:13.178
- Be careful, Na Ri! - Careful!

413
17:17.193 --> 17:18.928
Well done!

414
17:21.220 --> 17:23.042
Oh my God!

415
17:26.227 --> 17:28.333
I guess every dog has its day!

416
17:28.333 --> 17:31.669
He's giving Sergeant Shim a run for his money, no?

417
17:32.343 --> 17:34.105
Wow, Na Ri!

418
17:38.809 --> 17:40.268
Na Ri!

419
17:40.978 --> 17:42.308
You're our hope!

420
17:42.308 --> 17:43.552
Wipe it clean!

421
17:43.552 --> 17:45.455
Bit Na Ri, you saved us!

422
17:45.455 --> 17:47.453
Bit Na Ri, nice!

423
17:47.453 --> 17:49.017
Bit Na Ri, fighting!

424
17:49.017 --> 17:52.159
Private First Class Moon Bit Na Ri! Thank you!

425
18:08.208 --> 18:11.255
We're being swarmed from all sides by the enemy!

426
18:11.255 --> 18:13.139
Request an artillery strike right now!

427
18:13.139 --> 18:16.065
Coordinates are 322, 542! 322, 542!

428
18:16.065 --> 18:17.632
Requesting immediate fire!

429
18:17.632 --> 18:20.223
Enemies are assembling on the north ridge!

430
18:20.223 --> 18:22.561
Do you copy? Do you copy?

431
18:23.525 --> 18:25.164
Ah, for God's sake!

432
18:25.164 --> 18:26.509
We've lost communications!

433
18:26.509 --> 18:28.481
Where the hell is Moon Bit Na Ri?

434
18:28.481 --> 18:31.141
We're all gonna die out here!

435
18:31.141 --> 18:33.363
If Moon Bit Na Ri were here...

436
18:37.249 --> 18:39.671
Min Seok!

437
18:41.295 --> 18:42.657
Hold on a bit longer!

438
18:42.657 --> 18:44.121
Bit Na Ri is going to come!

439
18:44.121 --> 18:46.933
Min Seok, stay with us!

440
18:46.933 --> 18:49.003
We're done for.

441
18:49.003 --> 18:50.630
This is the end.

442
18:51.983 --> 18:54.009
Sergeant Kim Sang Hun.

443
18:54.791 --> 18:59.971
I will always cherish the memories of you as our squad leader!

444
18:59.971 --> 19:01.503
Stay with us!

445
19:01.503 --> 19:03.310
Park Min Seok!

446
19:03.310 --> 19:07.735
I'll be with you until the end!

447
19:08.462 --> 19:10.901
- Min Seok! - Love you!

448
19:13.156 --> 19:15.927
- Min Seok! - Min Seok!

449
19:15.927 --> 19:18.283
Oh, over there!

450
19:29.082 --> 19:31.221
It's Moon Bit Na Ri!

451
19:31.221 --> 19:33.888
- Moon Bit Na Ri has come! - Moon Bit Na Ri is here!

452
19:33.888 --> 19:36.043
We're saved!

453
19:46.629 --> 19:49.238
Oh, nice job, Bit Na Ri!

454
19:49.238 --> 19:50.562
Thank you!

455
19:50.562 --> 19:52.622
- You're built for crew-served weapons! - Yes, sir!

456
19:52.622 --> 19:54.229
Wow, well done, Bit Na Ri.

457
19:54.229 --> 19:56.227
Go over there first and get started.

458
19:56.227 --> 19:57.838
Yes, sir!

459
19:58.858 --> 20:00.326
Let's do this quickly!

460
20:00.326 --> 20:02.645
Yes, got it!

461
20:07.383 --> 20:09.167
If you finish fast, Kim Sang Hun will buy PX snacks!

462
20:09.167 --> 20:11.349
Oh, really?

463
20:11.349 --> 20:12.602
Okay, sure, I will.

464
20:12.602 --> 20:14.730
Hey, Bit Na Ri, look!

465
20:14.730 --> 20:15.957
Okay!

466
20:15.957 --> 20:18.140
No, look, look!

467
20:18.140 --> 20:19.151
I'm looking.

468
20:19.151 --> 20:21.095
No, I said look!

469
20:21.095 --> 20:23.015
You look nice, sir!

470
20:23.907 --> 20:26.484
You dumb-ass, look where you're cutting!

471
20:26.484 --> 20:28.504
Huh? Oh! No!

472
20:49.230 --> 20:50.445
We're fucked.

473
20:50.445 --> 20:52.712
Isn't this a ticket to the brig?

474
20:52.712 --> 20:55.436
For God's sake... Is he crazy?

475
20:57.214 --> 20:58.926
What's his problem?

476
21:08.987 --> 21:11.699
At this point, wouldn't green tape be better?

477
21:11.699 --> 21:13.672
- Yeah, it wouldn't be too obvious. - Right?

478
21:13.672 --> 21:16.235
I heard tonight's dinner is stir-fried pork...

479
21:16.235 --> 21:18.785
Did you do this on purpose to get lettuce wraps?

480
21:18.785 --> 21:20.984
- I'm sorry! - Be quiet and get on with it.

481
21:20.984 --> 21:23.450
Yes, understood, I'm sorry!

482
21:26.823 --> 21:29.977
But, what's the point of doing all this weed-whacking

483
21:29.977 --> 21:31.676
when we'll have to do it all again tomorrow?

484
21:31.676 --> 21:34.967
Wouldn't it be better to just buy weed-killer and sprinkle it all over?

485
21:34.967 --> 21:37.042
- Min Seok. - Corporal Park Min Seok.

486
21:37.042 --> 21:38.923
We're cheaper.

487
21:38.923 --> 21:40.039
Say that again, sorry?

488
21:40.039 --> 21:42.798
I said we're cheaper than weed killer.

489
21:42.798 --> 21:46.686
For the price of one bottle, they could probably hire ten more of us.

490
21:46.686 --> 21:48.073
How much do you make, Min Seok?

491
21:48.073 --> 21:50.267
Around 97,000 won a month?

492
21:50.267 --> 21:51.919
Excluding weekends...

493
21:51.919 --> 21:53.801
That's a daily rate of 4000 won a month.

494
21:53.801 --> 21:56.092
If you divide that by an 8-hour shift...

495
21:56.092 --> 21:58.692
Damn, it's 500 won an hour.

496
21:58.692 --> 22:00.263
No overtime pay either.

497
22:00.263 --> 22:01.918
Clocking out equals deserting.

498
22:01.918 --> 22:03.636
Still, at least we get room and board.

499
22:03.636 --> 22:05.275
Damn, 500 won...

500
22:05.275 --> 22:07.849
So, if we add all our wages up together,

501
22:07.849 --> 22:09.408
our hourly wage is...

502
22:09.408 --> 22:11.481
[4,000 won] Min Seok.

503
22:11.481 --> 22:13.488
Stop, I'm having an existential crisis.

504
22:13.488 --> 22:16.500
Yeah, sorry.

505
22:16.500 --> 22:18.653
Hey, hey!

506
22:18.653 --> 22:20.897
Dude, why are you putting it right against the ruler like that?

507
22:20.897 --> 22:22.581
The line will sever if you do it like this!

508
22:22.581 --> 22:23.688
This is basic common sense.

509
22:23.688 --> 22:26.322
Do I really need to walk you through this?

510
22:26.985 --> 22:29.374
Chungseong! Corporal Ji Jeong Min here on official business.

511
22:29.374 --> 22:30.829
We've come to pick up supplies.

512
22:30.829 --> 22:33.375
- Like what? - Work gloves.

513
22:33.375 --> 22:35.665
- Work gloves? - Yes.

514
22:35.665 --> 22:36.753
Here, go.

515
22:36.753 --> 22:37.903
There, off you go.

516
22:37.903 --> 22:40.103
But, what are you doing?

517
22:40.103 --> 22:42.331
What does it look like? Just wasting my time.

518
22:42.331 --> 22:45.288
Hey, "wasting time" is what we're doing out there today, covered in dust.

519
22:45.288 --> 22:46.901
Pulling out weeds is pointless.

520
22:46.901 --> 22:49.450
Sitting under a fan with scissors? That's luxury.

521
22:49.450 --> 22:50.457
Right.

522
22:50.457 --> 22:52.143
Wow, the attitudes of these guys...

523
22:52.143 --> 22:53.276
This is freaking difficult!

524
22:53.276 --> 22:55.534
You came here to protect the country, but you spend all day cutting paper.

525
22:55.534 --> 22:57.957
Admin guys really have it easy.

526
23:01.258 --> 23:02.820
Did you just say "easy?"

527
23:02.820 --> 23:05.297
Real talk, during morning roll call when it's boiling or freezing outside,

528
23:05.297 --> 23:07.221
all you have to do is stay inside and sort documents!

529
23:07.221 --> 23:08.671
Right, and you don't even have to stand night watch!

530
23:08.671 --> 23:10.540
I'm seriously so envious.

531
23:11.644 --> 23:13.851
Where the hell does this look "easy?"

532
23:13.851 --> 23:15.321
Instead of roll call,

533
23:15.321 --> 23:18.538
we get crushed under mountains of paper and get shredded by paper cuts.

534
23:18.538 --> 23:21.300
It hurts, it freaking hurts, do you know the pain?

535
23:21.300 --> 23:23.297
If your body's exhausted, at least you can sleep!

536
23:23.297 --> 23:25.587
I hear auditory hallucinations of Corporal No in my dreams

537
23:25.587 --> 23:28.432
screaming at me because one Excel cell didn't align!

538
23:28.432 --> 23:30.167
- That's not a dream. - Wait, what?

539
23:30.167 --> 23:31.670
You're getting chewed out today, too.

540
23:31.670 --> 23:35.413
Hey, at least you're nice and cool in summer and warm during winter!

541
23:35.413 --> 23:37.721
Wow, these guys really know nothing.

542
23:37.721 --> 23:39.749
Weather's not what's important.

543
23:39.749 --> 23:42.284
It's the officers' body temperatures that matter!

544
23:42.284 --> 23:45.437
First Sergeant, Platoon Leader, Assistant Platoon Leader!

545
23:45.437 --> 23:47.970
Look, if even one bubble gets under the contact paper?

546
23:47.970 --> 23:50.655
Your entire soul will be ripped apart.

547
23:52.598 --> 23:54.688
[Jeon]

548
23:54.688 --> 23:56.089
What the hell is this?

549
23:56.089 --> 23:57.666
It's all crooked!

550
23:57.666 --> 24:00.079
You must be all twisted and crooked, too.

551
24:00.079 --> 24:02.689
Your mind must be straight if you want your lines straight, kid!

552
24:02.689 --> 24:04.217
Sorry, I'll do it again!

553
24:04.217 --> 24:06.086
Hey, are you doing what I told you?

554
24:06.086 --> 24:08.095
Yes, I-I-I'm doing it!

555
24:08.095 --> 24:10.182
The guard duty rota's almost out...

556
24:10.182 --> 24:11.554
Take your time, go on.

557
24:11.554 --> 24:13.662
Though, guard duty reporting is around the corner.

558
24:13.662 --> 24:15.207
I-I-I'll get it done right away!

559
24:15.207 --> 24:17.463
You could've finished it in the time you were talking!

560
24:18.207 --> 24:19.680
Are you ignoring me?

561
24:19.680 --> 24:21.807
Hey, we really are in the advanced barracks now, huh?

562
24:21.807 --> 24:23.563
You said not to talk, so...

563
24:23.563 --> 24:25.209
We didn't say don't talk.

564
24:25.209 --> 24:26.426
We said that in the time you were talking,

565
24:26.426 --> 24:28.680
you could've finished by now, you idiot! Hurry up!

566
24:28.680 --> 24:30.295
You wanna go train instead?

567
24:30.295 --> 24:32.453
You're sitting under a fan, playing with scissors!

568
24:32.453 --> 24:34.154
Hurry the hell up, bastard, hurry!

569
24:34.154 --> 24:35.550
Yes, sorry, I'll hurry, sir.

570
24:35.550 --> 24:36.834
Your answers are half-assed!

571
24:36.834 --> 24:38.793
- And your work is half-assed, huh? - No, it's...

572
24:38.793 --> 24:40.576
No, it's going to go wrong if you do that...

573
24:40.576 --> 24:42.637
Are you out of your mind, hey, Sung Yoon Mo!

574
24:42.637 --> 24:44.216
- Sorry? - You can't even type right?

575
24:44.216 --> 24:45.225
Sorry, sir, sorry.

576
24:45.225 --> 24:46.714
- No Hee Jeong! - Sorry, sir!

577
24:46.714 --> 24:47.953
- Corporal No Hee Jeong! - Hey, Sung Yoon Mo!

578
24:47.953 --> 24:48.876
Corporal Sung Yoon Mo!

579
24:48.876 --> 24:50.024
- Sung Yoon Mo! - No Hee Jung!

580
24:50.024 --> 24:51.124
- Corporal No Hee Jeong! - Sung Yoon Mo!

581
24:51.124 --> 24:52.490
- Corporal Sung Yoon Mo! - No Hee Jeong!

582
24:52.490 --> 24:53.682
No, sir, if you push me like that, it'll...

583
24:53.682 --> 24:54.898
- Sun Yoon Mo! - No Hee Jeong!

584
24:54.898 --> 24:56.460
- Corporal Sung Yoon Mo! - No Hee Jeong!

585
24:56.460 --> 24:59.033
- I'm sorry! - I'm sorry!

586
24:59.033 --> 25:00.903
Not this, this!

587
25:00.903 --> 25:03.714
When the body has it easy, the mind is ripped apart.

588
25:04.505 --> 25:06.820
The mood swings and fickleness of these officers

589
25:06.820 --> 25:08.830
tear people to shreds.

590
25:08.830 --> 25:14.304
Making me start from goddamn scratch because one Excel cell doesn't line up!

591
25:14.304 --> 25:17.338
Whirr-clack, whirr-clack.

592
25:17.338 --> 25:19.160
Whirr-clack, whirr-clack!

593
25:19.160 --> 25:21.506
Whirr-clack, whirr-clack!

594
25:21.506 --> 25:24.482
Whirr-clack, whirr-clack!

595
25:24.482 --> 25:26.430
Do you know the horror of hearing those printers

596
25:26.430 --> 25:31.074
spitting out paper all night like they're screaming?

597
25:32.433 --> 25:34.321
I know this for a fact.

598
25:34.321 --> 25:36.952
Whatever, it's still a luxury.

599
25:36.952 --> 25:39.596
Okay, Yoon Mo, you've worked hard.

600
25:39.596 --> 25:41.225
Corporal No, you've worked hard too.

601
25:41.225 --> 25:43.735
Yeah, sure, we've got loads of things to do, so just go.

602
25:43.735 --> 25:46.466
Yes, sir, hang in there.

603
25:46.466 --> 25:47.851
Chungseong! Love you.

604
25:47.851 --> 25:50.267
Eat this whilst you're at it.

605
25:50.267 --> 25:52.079
We'll be off.

606
25:59.396 --> 26:00.996
Yoon Mo.

607
26:01.741 --> 26:03.476
Corporal Sung Yoon Mo.

608
26:03.476 --> 26:05.282
Well done.

609
26:05.282 --> 26:06.558
Thank you.

610
26:06.558 --> 26:09.152
What did I say the number one rule of being an admin clerk was?

611
26:09.152 --> 26:12.236
"You must always look exhausted in front of others."

612
26:12.236 --> 26:14.867
Exactly, and number two?

613
26:14.867 --> 26:17.153
"Don't forget rule one."

614
26:17.153 --> 26:18.284
Exactly.

615
26:18.284 --> 26:20.271
The second any of them hear that we have it easy,

616
26:20.271 --> 26:21.679
we'll get dragged out for training.

617
26:21.679 --> 26:25.372
You have to always be locked in with your method acting. Got it?

618
26:25.372 --> 26:27.004
Yes, understood.

619
26:27.004 --> 26:29.400
- Great. - So, then...

620
26:29.400 --> 26:32.900
To numb the pain for a moment, you wanna play Pikachu Volleyball?

621
26:32.900 --> 26:34.613
This bastard wants to play games during work hours...

622
26:34.613 --> 26:36.345
Of course!

623
26:36.345 --> 26:37.599
I'll be the right side.

624
26:37.599 --> 26:39.858
But you were right side last time, too.

625
26:39.858 --> 26:40.975
And so?

626
26:40.975 --> 26:42.373
Nothing, never mind.

627
26:42.373 --> 26:43.593
- I'm taking this, okay? - Sorry?

628
26:43.593 --> 26:45.266
He gave it to me.

629
26:45.974 --> 26:47.574
Hurry up!

630
26:49.771 --> 26:51.402
Bastard.

631
26:52.796 --> 26:54.260
Hey, you prepped everything, right?

632
26:54.260 --> 26:56.288
- Yes, sir! - Great, well done, guys.

633
26:56.288 --> 26:57.437
- Thank you! - Thank you!

634
26:57.437 --> 27:00.432
Hey, what are you doing bringing that out now? You should've already prepped it!

635
27:00.432 --> 27:02.218
- Sorry, sir. - For goodness sake.

636
27:02.218 --> 27:04.163
[Lieutenant Colonel Byeon Hyeok Jin, Commanding Officer, 7th Battalion]

637
27:05.188 --> 27:06.659
Okay, got it.

638
27:06.659 --> 27:08.504
Right, get ready!

639
27:11.797 --> 27:13.094
The Battalion Commander is here!

640
27:13.094 --> 27:16.073
Unit, attention!

641
27:17.334 --> 27:20.081
[Battalion Commander! Congratulations on Your Inauguration!]

642
27:23.900 --> 27:26.494
Salute to the Battalion Commander!

643
27:26.494 --> 27:28.423
- Chungseong! - Chungseong!

644
27:28.423 --> 27:29.448
Chungseong!

645
27:29.448 --> 27:31.338
Chungseong.

646
27:32.221 --> 27:33.547
Now.

647
27:34.642 --> 27:36.907
- At ease. - At ease.

648
27:38.072 --> 27:40.562
Wow, you guys prepared so much.

649
27:40.562 --> 27:43.718
It's just me, you didn't have to!

650
27:43.718 --> 27:46.944
The atmosphere of this unit is amazing! Thank you!

651
27:46.944 --> 27:49.280
Operations Officer, Major Kim Gwang Tae!

652
27:49.280 --> 27:52.217
All the battalion officers prepared this to welcome our new commander

653
27:52.217 --> 27:54.997
who chose to forgo his inauguration ceremony!

654
27:54.997 --> 27:56.021
Thank you.

655
27:56.021 --> 27:57.605
I heard you're the youngest lieutenant colonel.

656
27:57.605 --> 27:58.945
You're really amazing!

657
27:58.945 --> 28:01.457
I read your interview in Defense Daily and they called you

658
28:01.457 --> 28:03.520
"the rising star of the next generation of commanders."

659
28:03.520 --> 28:05.042
I'll learn a lot from you!

660
28:05.042 --> 28:06.787
Please, I'm the one who should work hard.

661
28:06.787 --> 28:09.954
A round of applause for the Battalion Commander!

662
28:14.825 --> 28:17.864
Yes, thank you. Hold on, wait, wait!

663
28:20.795 --> 28:23.246
But, if all the battalion officers are here,

664
28:23.246 --> 28:24.863
then who's keeping an eye on things?

665
28:24.863 --> 28:26.496
We left essential personnel behind.

666
28:26.496 --> 28:28.311
- "Essential personnel?" - Ah, yes.

667
28:28.311 --> 28:30.261
There are admin staff and operations specialists

668
28:30.261 --> 28:33.120
from each company monitoring things in the control center.

669
28:33.120 --> 28:35.262
The "essential personnel..."

670
28:35.262 --> 28:38.543
So, then, are there "non-essential personnel" in our unit?

671
28:38.543 --> 28:40.017
Sorry?

672
28:44.339 --> 28:46.634
Ah, that's...

673
28:46.634 --> 28:49.965
We heard you were coming, so we all came here to congratulate you.

674
28:49.965 --> 28:51.702
We've always done it this way.

675
28:51.702 --> 28:53.571
Ah, "always done it".

676
28:53.571 --> 28:55.901
It's always been like this?

677
28:55.901 --> 28:56.997
- Sorry? - It's a tradition

678
28:56.997 --> 29:00.928
for battalion officers to leave their posts unattended and come gather like this?

679
29:04.364 --> 29:06.361
Lieutenant Colonel, I understand what you're saying,

680
29:06.361 --> 29:10.438
but today's your welcome ceremony, and for our officers' morale, well...

681
29:10.438 --> 29:12.169
"Officers' morale?"

682
29:12.944 --> 29:15.474
Then, what about the soldiers' morale?

683
29:15.474 --> 29:17.334
All the food and the banners prepared here today,

684
29:17.334 --> 29:18.943
did you all personally prepare them?

685
29:18.943 --> 29:21.293
You didn't order the soldiers to do it?

686
29:21.293 --> 29:23.927
Is it any wonder that soldiers joke that

687
29:23.927 --> 29:26.932
their real enemies are their own officers?

688
29:28.667 --> 29:34.019
I think that soldiers' morale comes from trust.

689
29:34.019 --> 29:36.465
Trusting the commanding officers in this room.

690
29:36.465 --> 29:40.307
Trusting your peers beside you, and through that, trusting the organization.

691
29:41.262 --> 29:43.236
If you break that trust,

692
29:43.236 --> 29:45.585
the strength of the army crumbles, too.

693
29:46.681 --> 29:50.986
A military where we can trust each other, thus a military everyone can trust.

694
29:50.986 --> 29:53.958
Whilst I am here, I am going to make all of these changes.

695
29:53.958 --> 29:57.802
To the military, to all of you, everything.

696
29:59.308 --> 30:01.284
Do you understand?

697
30:01.284 --> 30:03.273
- Yes, sir! - Yes, sir!

698
30:03.273 --> 30:07.766
I'll accept the gesture from the officers who prepared this today.

699
30:07.766 --> 30:10.503
The soldiers diligently prepared this,

700
30:10.503 --> 30:12.610
so please enjoy!

701
30:31.481 --> 30:33.624
- Hyeon Uk. - Private Kim Hyeon Uk!

702
30:33.624 --> 30:36.045
- Was today your first night watch? - Yes, that's correct.

703
30:36.045 --> 30:38.504
- Oh, come, sit down! - Okay.

704
30:39.383 --> 30:40.986
So, the night watch, well...

705
30:40.986 --> 30:43.226
I did it at training camp, so it's nothing special.

706
30:43.226 --> 30:45.127
So just, I guess, how to be a bit careful?

707
30:45.127 --> 30:47.311
- I'll tell you a few ways. - Okay, great.

708
30:47.311 --> 30:48.958
First, if a senior wakes you up,

709
30:48.958 --> 30:52.377
get up immediately, change, and take over right away.

710
30:52.377 --> 30:55.304
Anyone on guard duty needs to be woken up 30 minutes early though.

711
30:55.304 --> 30:56.714
Oh, and when you wake them up,

712
30:56.714 --> 30:59.073
never touch the senior like this, never, okay?

713
30:59.073 --> 31:00.643
Just go up to their side quietly,

714
31:00.643 --> 31:03.016
"Corporal Park Min Seok, it's time for guard duty.

715
31:03.016 --> 31:05.566
You have to wake up." Wake them like this, okay?

716
31:05.566 --> 31:06.806
- Yes, got it. - If you're too loud,

717
31:06.806 --> 31:09.199
you'll wake everyone else, and they'll curse you out so bad.

718
31:09.199 --> 31:11.347
- You've got to be really careful, okay? - Yes, understood.

719
31:11.347 --> 31:13.889
Oh, and if you're checking the room temperature and it's too hot,

720
31:13.889 --> 31:16.920
you can sprinkle some water on the floor like this.

721
31:16.920 --> 31:20.531
But again, be super careful not to splash any on their boots, yeah?

722
31:20.531 --> 31:21.630
Yes, got it.

723
31:21.630 --> 31:22.798
What else...

724
31:22.798 --> 31:26.858
Oh, you'll sometimes come across people who snore really loudly.

725
31:26.858 --> 31:28.762
In that case, don't wake them up,

726
31:28.762 --> 31:29.990
but there's this pillow, right?

727
31:29.990 --> 31:32.458
You can just nudge it, gently though.

728
31:32.458 --> 31:33.993
- That should work. - Okay, got it.

729
31:33.993 --> 31:36.175
Yeah, that's pretty much it? Not hard, right?

730
31:36.175 --> 31:37.276
- No, sir, it isn't. - Yeah.

731
31:37.276 --> 31:38.981
If you get into a bind,

732
31:38.981 --> 31:41.198
or something goes wrong, go straight to admin...

733
31:41.198 --> 31:44.189
No, just wake me, actually.

734
31:44.189 --> 31:46.669
- I couldn't. - No, it's all good, you can!

735
31:46.669 --> 31:47.717
Got it?

736
31:47.717 --> 31:49.621
- Okay, I understand. - Cool.

737
31:49.621 --> 31:51.143
I mean, you always do well, so.

738
31:51.143 --> 31:52.492
- Thank you. - You wrote it all down?

739
31:52.492 --> 31:54.087
Yes.

740
31:54.087 --> 31:56.203
- Hello, sir! - Yeah.

741
31:56.203 --> 31:57.912
You trained him well, right?

742
31:57.912 --> 31:59.371
Yes, sir, I did.

743
31:59.371 --> 32:01.265
- Learned a lot? - Yes, sir, I did.

744
32:01.265 --> 32:04.968
Wow, I remember Park Min Seok's first night watch.

745
32:04.968 --> 32:07.117
It's hard to forget.

746
32:07.117 --> 32:09.098
Oh? What happened?

747
32:09.098 --> 32:11.057
Hey, Moon Bit Na Ri, be quiet.

748
32:11.057 --> 32:13.414
Come on, what's the big deal, dude?

749
32:13.414 --> 32:15.267
Back then...

750
32:20.962 --> 32:22.092
What is it again?

751
32:22.092 --> 32:24.573
[Temperature Reading] [Barracks No.1]

752
32:24.573 --> 32:25.968
Crap...

753
32:25.968 --> 32:27.446
Do I have to report this?

754
32:27.446 --> 32:30.486
Damn it, I've just got to do it.

755
32:30.486 --> 32:31.630
Where are you going, punk?

756
32:31.630 --> 32:33.502
Oh, Corporal Choi Il Gu.

757
32:33.502 --> 32:35.264
Have you checked the temperature and everything?

758
32:35.264 --> 32:37.542
Yes, I've done the temperature readings, but...

759
32:37.542 --> 32:39.858
But what? Is there something unusual?

760
32:39.858 --> 32:41.914
There's an empty cot.

761
32:41.914 --> 32:43.291
What?

762
32:43.291 --> 32:44.581
I didn't see anyone go, though?

763
32:44.581 --> 32:46.464
- What barrack? - Barrack one, sir.

764
32:46.464 --> 32:48.470
- Barrack one? - Yes.

765
32:50.125 --> 32:52.265
Wait, is that not your cot?

766
32:54.843 --> 32:56.892
Right, yes, that's right!

767
32:56.892 --> 32:59.136
Wow, I was worried.

768
32:59.136 --> 33:01.840
Wow, it was so fucking funny.

769
33:01.840 --> 33:02.906
I remember.

770
33:02.906 --> 33:05.415
They're all old stories now, no?

771
33:07.462 --> 33:09.411
Hey, Moon Bit Na Ri, mind your face.

772
33:09.411 --> 33:10.853
Sorry, sir.

773
33:10.853 --> 33:12.470
You're smiling?

774
33:12.470 --> 33:14.402
I'll give you something to smile about!

775
33:14.402 --> 33:16.142
- You're smiling, huh? - I'm not!

776
33:16.142 --> 33:19.030
Hey, what are you doing!

777
33:19.030 --> 33:20.951
- Did you really learn anything? - Yes, I did, sir!

778
33:20.951 --> 33:22.938
- Okay. - Get over here. Hyeon Uk, grab him!

779
33:22.938 --> 33:25.253
Private Kim Hyeon Uk! Okay...

780
33:25.253 --> 33:27.758
- Guys, calm down. - Take care, sir. Goodbye!

781
33:27.758 --> 33:30.622
Grab him now, quickly, quickly!

782
33:38.888 --> 33:41.324
- Hey. - Private Kim Hyeon Uk!

783
33:41.324 --> 33:43.856
- Get ready. - Okay, sir.

784
34:45.788 --> 34:47.577
Oh, I'm gonna die.

785
34:47.577 --> 34:49.136
Hey, Sang Hun, what time is it?

786
34:49.136 --> 34:51.124
Right now it's 3:45 a.m.

787
34:51.124 --> 34:52.838
Oh?

788
34:53.562 --> 34:55.430
Wait...

789
34:55.430 --> 34:57.334
Why haven't those punks come to swap guard posts?

790
34:57.334 --> 34:59.596
I'll go check the night watch now.

791
35:00.608 --> 35:01.853
[Guard Post Hotline]

792
35:01.853 --> 35:03.772
Go out and check!

793
35:03.772 --> 35:05.278
Yes, sir!

794
35:05.952 --> 35:08.150
This is communications security. Okay.

795
35:08.150 --> 35:10.463
Yeah, I'm already looking into it, okay.

796
35:10.463 --> 35:12.879
I'll sort it out right now and send them. Hang in there a bit longer.

797
35:12.879 --> 35:14.661
Yeah, sorry.

798
35:16.327 --> 35:19.410
These goddamn slackers, 15 minutes late...

799
35:20.571 --> 35:24.021
Fucking hell, these bastards.

800
35:24.021 --> 35:26.292
Hey, which night watch bastard...

801
35:27.254 --> 35:29.110
Private Kim Hyeon Uk!

802
35:29.110 --> 35:31.049
I'm sorry!

803
35:31.049 --> 35:32.589
Hey, where's his mentor?

804
35:32.589 --> 35:33.890
Corporal Yoon Joon Young.

805
35:33.890 --> 35:36.525
I'm sorry, I should've woken you!

806
35:37.556 --> 35:39.838
Go wake all the squad leaders.

807
35:40.659 --> 35:43.103
- Could you repeat that, sir? - You heard me.

808
35:43.103 --> 35:44.931
Go wake the squad leaders and bring them here.

809
35:44.931 --> 35:46.596
Okay, sir!

810
35:48.817 --> 35:51.407
Jesus, and here I thought that bastard was an ace.

811
35:51.407 --> 35:53.105
Corporal Yoon Joon Young...

812
35:53.105 --> 35:55.194
- Is this right? - No, sir.

813
35:55.194 --> 35:57.763
- Well? Is it? - I'm sorry, sir.

814
36:05.041 --> 36:06.659
Time to get up!

815
36:09.149 --> 36:10.836
Rise and shine!

816
36:18.013 --> 36:19.255
Hey, it was you, right?

817
36:19.255 --> 36:21.308
Private Kim Hyeon Uk!

818
36:21.308 --> 36:22.524
I apologize.

819
36:22.524 --> 36:25.645
Hey, Min Seok, get your mentee under control.

820
36:25.645 --> 36:26.983
Hey, Im Da Hye.

821
36:26.983 --> 36:28.813
Sort out your new recruit.

822
36:29.462 --> 36:30.480
Sorry, sir.

823
36:30.480 --> 36:32.831
For God's sake.

824
36:32.831 --> 36:34.675
I'm sorry.

825
36:34.675 --> 36:36.320
Take care.

826
36:40.352 --> 36:42.749
Even though you're a private,

827
36:42.749 --> 36:44.789
I thought you'd be different than the others.

828
36:44.789 --> 36:47.336
Seriously, I trusted you, what the hell?

829
36:47.336 --> 36:49.685
- I'm sorry. - I told you to wake me

830
36:49.685 --> 36:52.958
if something was confusing or seemed off!

831
36:52.958 --> 36:54.834
Wait, you didn't doze off, did you?

832
36:54.834 --> 36:56.566
No, it really wasn't that...

833
36:56.566 --> 36:58.009
I mistook the time...

834
36:58.009 --> 37:01.437
And here I was praising you, what a mess.

835
37:01.437 --> 37:03.759
I'm gonna smoke this like a boss!

836
37:03.759 --> 37:05.201
Good morning.

837
37:05.201 --> 37:06.527
Park Min Seok, giving a lecture?

838
37:06.527 --> 37:07.894
[Smoking Area] It's not the private's fault, is it?

839
37:07.894 --> 37:09.602
The teacher's in the wrong.

840
37:09.602 --> 37:10.699
No...

841
37:10.699 --> 37:13.249
Corporal Park taught me well. It was my mistake.

842
37:13.249 --> 37:15.496
Oh, covering for your senior, too?

843
37:15.496 --> 37:17.018
Park Min Seok, you're really something, huh?

844
37:17.018 --> 37:18.797
Handing down your screw-ups, too?

845
37:18.797 --> 37:20.070
No, really, it wasn't his fault.

846
37:20.070 --> 37:21.222
I got the time wrong.

847
37:21.222 --> 37:24.690
Oh, Ace Kim Hyeon Uk!

848
37:24.690 --> 37:27.758
Damn it, you should've been with me instead of Min Seok.

849
37:27.758 --> 37:30.015
Hey, seriously, do better next time.

850
37:30.015 --> 37:32.246
Yes, I will!

851
37:32.246 --> 37:33.740
Finally acting like a senior soldier!

852
37:33.740 --> 37:36.221
Why are you guys like this?

853
37:36.221 --> 37:37.402
Got it?

854
37:37.402 --> 37:40.280
- Yes, sir. - Ten minutes until roll call!

855
37:40.280 --> 37:42.793
- Let's go. - Okay, let's head in.

856
37:42.793 --> 37:46.046
Looking at this bastard act, I can't believe I'm getting discharged.

857
37:46.046 --> 37:47.879
Do better next time, I'm serious.

858
37:47.879 --> 37:49.369
I will, sir.

859
37:49.369 --> 37:50.769
Okay.

860
37:52.481 --> 37:54.848
Yes, firstly...

861
37:54.848 --> 37:57.260
Have the operations officers run the meeting.

862
37:57.260 --> 38:00.904
Yes, I'll get the report when I get there.

863
38:00.904 --> 38:02.744
Yes.

864
38:02.744 --> 38:06.278
Right, take care, then.

865
38:06.921 --> 38:08.584
Lieutenant Colonel Byeon!

866
38:08.584 --> 38:11.228
Fancy seeing you here!

867
38:11.228 --> 38:12.831
Chungseong.

868
38:16.089 --> 38:17.689
Chungseong.

869
38:23.091 --> 38:25.012
It's been a while.

870
38:25.012 --> 38:27.306
Yes, it's good to see you again.

871
38:40.357 --> 38:43.144
I'm so tired!

872
38:43.144 --> 38:44.487
Did your shift go well?

873
38:44.487 --> 38:46.776
Of course it did, punk.

874
38:47.396 --> 38:48.930
Hey, Bit Na Ri, what's for breakfast today?

875
38:48.930 --> 38:51.358
Today's stir-fried sausage and vegetables, and poop soup!

876
38:51.358 --> 38:53.391
Poop soup, again?

877
38:54.464 --> 38:56.501
- Snag the chocolate milk! - I will.

878
38:56.501 --> 38:58.782
Corporal Sung Yoon Mo. Reporting for duty at barracks one!

879
38:58.782 --> 39:00.674
- Can I enter? - Come in.

880
39:02.445 --> 39:04.411
- What is it? - Right, so...

881
39:04.411 --> 39:07.336
Effective today, you're on mess hall duty for Second Company.

882
39:07.336 --> 39:08.967
What the hell is he saying?

883
39:08.967 --> 39:10.055
"Mess hall duty?"

884
39:10.055 --> 39:11.145
Yes, that's correct.

885
39:11.145 --> 39:13.426
It's so tedious, though.

886
39:13.426 --> 39:14.686
Da Hye, you go.

887
39:14.686 --> 39:15.716
Min Seok.

888
39:15.716 --> 39:16.734
Moon Bit Na Ri.

889
39:16.734 --> 39:18.644
Hyeon Uk, oh?

890
39:18.644 --> 39:21.139
The privates went off earlier to do a survey, remember?

891
39:21.139 --> 39:22.621
Right...

892
39:24.559 --> 39:26.272
"Right?"

893
39:26.272 --> 39:28.270
What, it's already too tedious for you?

894
39:28.270 --> 39:29.910
Private First Class, Moon Bit Na Ri. No, sir!

895
39:29.910 --> 39:31.941
This bastard's slacking so much.

896
39:31.941 --> 39:33.593
Who's going to teach him?

897
39:33.593 --> 39:37.024
The teacher...

898
39:38.626 --> 39:40.229
Damn, this shit reeks!

899
39:40.229 --> 39:42.444
Go scrub the food bins.

900
39:42.444 --> 39:44.646
Why the hell do they need an officer for this?

901
39:44.646 --> 39:46.361
I really don't get it.

902
39:46.361 --> 39:48.713
Are you even trying? Use your muscles!

903
39:48.713 --> 39:49.946
I'm sorry!

904
39:49.946 --> 39:53.296
It's so damn heavy, there's so much food waste.

905
39:53.296 --> 39:55.391
The menu was trash, right?

906
39:55.391 --> 39:56.915
I liked it!

907
39:56.915 --> 39:58.273
What was nice about it?

908
39:58.273 --> 40:02.720
Sausages with vegetables, beef bulgogi, squid and radish soup!

909
40:02.720 --> 40:05.291
Seaweed soup, stir-fried potatoes, seaweed snacks.

910
40:05.291 --> 40:08.601
And honestly, they should always do the tteok dumpling soup!

911
40:08.601 --> 40:10.806
Is there anything you don't find delicious?

912
40:10.806 --> 40:12.100
Nothing so far!

913
40:12.100 --> 40:14.581
If there's nothing so far, there won't be anything!

914
40:14.581 --> 40:16.391
Hey, stop, stop!

915
40:19.211 --> 40:22.067
If everyone were like Bit Na Ri, cooking would be worth it.

916
40:22.067 --> 40:25.133
But honestly, I like everything you guys make!

917
40:25.133 --> 40:27.842
Really? Then why don't you become a cook?

918
40:27.842 --> 40:31.220
I mean, the food storehouse is packed, and you can eat all the sausages you want.

919
40:31.220 --> 40:32.541
Wait... really?

920
40:32.541 --> 40:34.873
- Of course! - Hey, leave the kid alone.

921
40:34.873 --> 40:36.951
Don't let him fool you, he's an elite.

922
40:36.951 --> 40:38.789
So people with high credentials can't be mess hall cooks?

923
40:38.789 --> 40:40.104
I graduated college, too!

924
40:40.104 --> 40:43.072
Damn, I feel alienated suddenly.

925
40:48.810 --> 40:51.245
Squad, attention!

926
40:51.245 --> 40:53.970
Salute to the Mess Hall Tiger!

927
40:53.970 --> 40:56.321
Chungseong! Love...

928
40:58.192 --> 41:00.840
Why are you joking around, Staff Sergeant Choi?

929
41:00.840 --> 41:04.423
Hey, he outranks you, idiot, it's only right for you to salute him!

930
41:04.423 --> 41:07.565
- Damn right. - I'm not a cat though!

931
41:09.136 --> 41:12.221
Is the old man coming?

932
41:12.221 --> 41:13.302
What old man?

933
41:13.302 --> 41:14.586
The waste removal man.

934
41:14.586 --> 41:16.013
You know that, right?

935
41:16.013 --> 41:19.337
That there are only two vehicles that get a free pass through our main gate?

936
41:19.337 --> 41:21.406
Wait, is that true?

937
41:24.652 --> 41:25.910
The waste removal man's truck.

938
41:25.910 --> 41:27.803
- And the vending machine lady. - Goodness, it's boiling.

939
41:27.803 --> 41:29.872
Open sesame!

940
41:29.872 --> 41:31.954
Nice.

941
41:31.954 --> 41:33.131
Chungseong! Love you!

942
41:33.131 --> 41:34.244
My goodness!

943
41:34.244 --> 41:35.424
You're back from leave?

944
41:35.424 --> 41:36.648
Yes, ma'am!

945
41:36.648 --> 41:37.932
What did you get up to?

946
41:37.932 --> 41:39.941
I broke up with my girlfriend.

947
41:39.941 --> 41:42.848
Hey, why the long face? You'll see her again!

948
41:42.848 --> 41:43.912
- Thank you. - Of course.

949
41:43.912 --> 41:45.146
Have a good day!

950
41:45.146 --> 41:47.767
Wow, that's so interesting!

951
41:47.767 --> 41:50.302
Wait, but where does the food waste go?

952
41:50.302 --> 41:53.043
This? A pig farm, I reckon?

953
41:53.043 --> 41:56.335
From what I've heard, the old man doesn't actually own a farm.

954
41:56.335 --> 41:58.967
Wait, then what does he do with all this slop?

955
41:58.967 --> 42:00.513
Well, it's just something I heard.

956
42:00.513 --> 42:02.163
I'm not certain.

957
42:02.768 --> 42:03.962
I think that's him there!

958
42:03.962 --> 42:06.501
Okay, he's coming. Stop, stop.

959
42:09.242 --> 42:10.509
Chungseong! Love you!

960
42:10.509 --> 42:12.131
Good job!

961
42:18.092 --> 42:19.887
Why are you so late, sir?

962
42:19.887 --> 42:21.917
Damn, my hip!

963
42:21.917 --> 42:25.176
I had some business to do. I was a bit busy!

964
42:25.176 --> 42:26.210
You got a problem?

965
42:26.210 --> 42:29.329
No, but, I feel like your mustache gets longer every time we meet!

966
42:29.329 --> 42:30.638
Damn, this punk!

967
42:30.638 --> 42:33.289
You got promoted to sergeant, now you're running your mouth, huh?

968
42:33.289 --> 42:35.584
"Sir!"

969
42:35.584 --> 42:37.930
"Please, can I have a cigarette?"

970
42:37.930 --> 42:39.496
Feels like just yesterday.

971
42:39.496 --> 42:41.566
You've gotten pretty cocky, Choi Il Gu!

972
42:41.566 --> 42:43.980
Me? Since when?

973
42:44.571 --> 42:46.261
Wait, who's this? A new recruit?

974
42:46.261 --> 42:47.846
Private First Class Moon Bit Na Ri!

975
42:47.846 --> 42:50.199
- You're "Private First Class?" - Yes, that's right!

976
42:50.199 --> 42:53.543
You bastard, it took you getting to that rank to finally report to me, huh?

977
42:53.543 --> 42:55.841
I'm sorry!

978
42:55.841 --> 42:57.412
Attention!

979
42:57.412 --> 42:58.790
At ease.

980
42:58.790 --> 43:00.063
Attention!

981
43:00.063 --> 43:01.915
At ease.

982
43:01.915 --> 43:03.953
- Moon Bit Na Ri. - Private First Class Moon Bit Na Ri!

983
43:03.953 --> 43:06.125
Where's all your spark, huh?

984
43:06.125 --> 43:07.920
It's...

985
43:08.599 --> 43:10.428
Okay, enough.

986
43:10.428 --> 43:13.101
I don't know how well you can do in the military, but do well.

987
43:13.101 --> 43:14.665
If you have any problems, call me!

988
43:14.665 --> 43:15.936
Not that I'll be much help, but...

989
43:15.936 --> 43:18.420
Yes, okay, sir!

990
43:18.420 --> 43:20.541
Wow, this is heavy.

991
43:21.333 --> 43:22.660
I said, it's heavy.

992
43:22.660 --> 43:25.451
Right, yeah, I'll help!

993
43:26.364 --> 43:27.783
One, two...

994
43:27.783 --> 43:28.927
- Choi Il Gu. - Yes?

995
43:28.927 --> 43:30.044
What are you doing?

996
43:30.044 --> 43:33.530
I was getting to it. Why are you rushing me?

997
43:35.655 --> 43:39.024
Look at this guy.

998
43:39.024 --> 43:41.981
It's totally covered in slop.

999
43:42.703 --> 43:44.126
- A little help! - Yes, sir!

1000
43:44.126 --> 43:45.929
One, two, three!

1001
43:47.124 --> 43:49.665
Wow, I remember when Choi was clueless.

1002
43:49.665 --> 43:54.178
Now look at him, he should be running the unit!

1003
43:54.178 --> 43:55.409
Well done, boys!

1004
43:55.409 --> 43:57.385
- Yes, head in. - Yes, yes.

1005
43:57.385 --> 43:58.447
But...

1006
43:58.447 --> 43:59.735
no salute?

1007
43:59.735 --> 44:01.668
Right... Chungseong! Love you!

1008
44:01.668 --> 44:03.734
Chungseong! Love you!

1009
44:03.734 --> 44:06.958
By the way, last time the pork was a bit salty.

1010
44:06.958 --> 44:08.346
Keep that in mind!

1011
44:08.346 --> 44:09.454
Yes, understood.

1012
44:09.454 --> 44:11.120
- Good work. - Yes, drive safely.

1013
44:11.120 --> 44:12.818
- Goodbye! - Goodbye!

1014
44:16.187 --> 44:18.118
- You heard him, keep it in mind! - Yes, sir.

1015
44:18.118 --> 44:19.363
Let's go.

1016
44:19.363 --> 44:22.356
Wait, don't you think that was a bit strange?

1017
44:22.356 --> 44:25.087
- What was? - That he said it was too salty?

1018
44:25.087 --> 44:28.081
Doesn't that mean he's tried it?

1019
44:28.860 --> 44:30.419
Wait.

1020
44:30.419 --> 44:33.478
From what I've heard, the old man doesn't actually own a farm.

1021
44:33.478 --> 44:35.299
Then what does he do with all this slop?

1022
44:35.299 --> 44:38.306
The pork was a bit salty, keep that in mind!

1023
44:38.306 --> 44:39.613
What?

1024
44:41.031 --> 44:42.631
No way...

1025
44:47.746 --> 44:49.067
The vending machine tastes different.

1026
44:49.067 --> 44:50.818
- That's because you're getting discharged! - Oh?

1027
44:50.818 --> 44:52.769
Chungseong! Love you.

1028
44:53.720 --> 44:55.809
This guy's acting sketch.

1029
44:57.036 --> 44:58.190
Hey!

1030
44:58.190 --> 44:59.777
Corporal Sung Yoon Mo!

1031
44:59.777 --> 45:01.047
What's this?

1032
45:01.047 --> 45:02.708
[Guard Duty] Why are we on guard duty?

1033
45:02.708 --> 45:05.549
Why would they put two last-years together?

1034
45:05.549 --> 45:06.581
Hey, you bastard.

1035
45:06.581 --> 45:08.706
Even the base cats could get past two final-years on guard duty.

1036
45:08.706 --> 45:10.177
Might as well be a revolving door!

1037
45:10.177 --> 45:13.041
What if we trip and twist an ankle going up the stairs, huh?

1038
45:13.041 --> 45:15.435
This is unbelievable, seriously.

1039
45:15.435 --> 45:17.847
Did the Company Commander or First Sergeant say anything about this?

1040
45:17.847 --> 45:19.394
Like "excuse them from watch" or something?

1041
45:19.394 --> 45:21.450
They didn't say anything.

1042
45:21.450 --> 45:24.752
They just said to put you two on duty because so many people are on leave.

1043
45:24.752 --> 45:26.940
Hey, No Wan Yong!

1044
45:26.940 --> 45:28.735
Corporal No Wan Yong.

1045
45:28.735 --> 45:31.521
You get it, right? Go talk to them and get our shifts covered.

1046
45:31.521 --> 45:33.295
Yes, I will go talk to them.

1047
45:33.295 --> 45:35.021
That bastard knew all along.

1048
45:35.021 --> 45:37.661
- Let's go. - Yeah.

1049
45:37.661 --> 45:39.693
Have a good day.

1050
45:39.693 --> 45:41.471
Take care.

1051
45:48.413 --> 45:49.676
You!

1052
45:49.676 --> 45:51.611
Raise that finger again and you're dead meat, seriously!

1053
45:51.611 --> 45:53.304
No, I-I didn't, really!

1054
45:53.304 --> 45:54.683
You thought we didn't know, huh?

1055
45:54.683 --> 45:56.018
I-I really didn't do that!

1056
45:56.018 --> 45:57.433
But... there's something behind you!

1057
45:57.433 --> 45:58.631
Watch your own back, bastard!

1058
45:58.631 --> 46:01.784
No, I mean, there's something there! I'm just telling you, it's...

1059
46:04.209 --> 46:06.182
I-I did clearly t-tell you.

1060
46:06.182 --> 46:08.724
Jesus, so embarrassing.

1061
46:08.724 --> 46:10.604
Hey, Sung Yoon Mo, clean this up!

1062
46:10.604 --> 46:12.913
Y-Yes, okay.

1063
46:13.857 --> 46:16.584
When will those bastards get discharged?

1064
46:27.642 --> 46:30.454
Command Sergeant Major. Chungseong! Love you!

1065
46:38.504 --> 46:41.202
Sorry, I'll clean it up right now!

1066
46:44.346 --> 46:45.487
Yes, sir!

1067
46:45.487 --> 46:46.582
Chungseong! Love you!

1068
46:46.582 --> 46:48.067
Okay.

1069
46:51.793 --> 46:53.773
Corporal No Hee Jeong.

1070
46:53.773 --> 46:55.236
What?

1071
46:56.207 --> 46:58.976
How did you understand that?

1072
46:58.976 --> 47:00.676
- What? - Not gonna lie,

1073
47:00.676 --> 47:02.432
I couldn't understand a word he said.

1074
47:02.432 --> 47:04.139
I see.

1075
47:04.139 --> 47:05.837
- Me neither. - Wait, what?

1076
47:05.837 --> 47:08.280
I think I misheard you.

1077
47:08.280 --> 47:11.569
There's no one in our unit who can fully understand what he's saying.

1078
47:11.569 --> 47:12.695
Then, how...

1079
47:12.695 --> 47:14.825
You think these years of seniority mean nothing, huh?

1080
47:14.825 --> 47:16.895
- Sorry? - Just listen closely, okay?

1081
47:16.895 --> 47:19.379
Just pick up the key words.

1082
47:19.379 --> 47:21.190
Look, what did he say earlier?

1083
47:21.190 --> 47:22.476
Euugh...

1084
47:22.476 --> 47:23.851
I-I'm not sure.

1085
47:23.851 --> 47:24.926
"Blah blah blah, fallen leaves."

1086
47:24.926 --> 47:25.875
Euugh... fallen leaves...

1087
47:25.875 --> 47:27.241
"Blah blah blah, central corridor."

1088
47:27.241 --> 47:28.350
Eugghhh... central corridor...

1089
47:28.350 --> 47:30.264
"Blah blah blah..." then what?

1090
47:30.264 --> 47:31.273
Eugh... with a broom!

1091
47:31.273 --> 47:32.310
With a broom.

1092
47:32.310 --> 47:34.290
I'm n-not sure.

1093
47:34.290 --> 47:36.214
"Broom," you dimwit, a broom!

1094
47:36.214 --> 47:37.949
That's how you piece it together.

1095
47:37.949 --> 47:40.586
What's a "broom?"

1096
47:40.586 --> 47:41.743
You're so...

1097
47:41.743 --> 47:43.705
Do you live your life without using your brain?

1098
47:43.705 --> 47:46.339
Just floating through life, not a single thought in your head?

1099
47:46.339 --> 47:49.408
Connect the dots, man, it's the thing you sweep the floor with!

1100
47:49.408 --> 47:51.954
Oh, that thing!

1101
47:51.954 --> 47:53.796
Makes sense now, huh?

1102
47:53.796 --> 47:57.532
The main corridor is filthy from all those leaves,

1103
47:57.532 --> 48:01.760
so keep a broom with you and clean up whenever you see them.

1104
48:01.760 --> 48:02.880
- Okay? - Got it.

1105
48:02.880 --> 48:04.240
- Yoon Mo. - Yes?

1106
48:04.240 --> 48:05.159
Yoon Mo.

1107
48:05.159 --> 48:06.105
- What? - Okay?

1108
48:06.105 --> 48:07.440
- Sorry? - Got it?

1109
48:07.440 --> 48:08.706
- What? - Okay?

1110
48:08.706 --> 48:09.973
Right, got it.

1111
48:09.973 --> 48:11.466
Damn it.

1112
48:11.466 --> 48:13.425
I'm going to go sort this out, so stay here, don't move.

1113
48:13.425 --> 48:14.475
Yes, sir.

1114
48:14.475 --> 48:16.140
Don't mess up, okay?

1115
48:16.140 --> 48:17.187
Yes, sir.

1116
48:17.187 --> 48:18.986
Goodness me.

1117
48:24.464 --> 48:26.091
So clever.

1118
48:29.871 --> 48:32.497
I'm going to make a unit cafe.

1119
48:35.749 --> 48:38.120
What sort of cafe, sir?

1120
48:39.023 --> 48:41.234
Not a cafe for coffee.

1121
48:41.234 --> 48:44.670
An online one, Daum Cafe.

1122
48:44.670 --> 48:49.608
Where parents can sign up and see how our soldiers are holding up.

1123
48:49.608 --> 48:52.360
Battalion Commander, it's a bit tricky in terms of security...

1124
48:52.360 --> 48:54.399
- Second Company Commander. - Yes, sir.

1125
48:54.399 --> 48:57.259
Does a little risk stop you from getting things done?

1126
48:57.259 --> 48:59.169
No, sir.

1127
48:59.815 --> 49:02.178
The military has to change.

1128
49:02.178 --> 49:04.387
This place needs to change if it's going to grow, too.

1129
49:04.387 --> 49:06.048
Until now, everything's been buried,

1130
49:06.048 --> 49:09.559
covered up, and hidden under the guise of "security."

1131
49:09.559 --> 49:13.244
We're not talking about top-secret intel that could leak to enemy forces.

1132
49:13.984 --> 49:19.338
Parents deserve to know how their boys are faring in here, that's what I think.

1133
49:19.338 --> 49:21.384
Yes, that's right.

1134
49:21.384 --> 49:22.769
Good.

1135
49:23.512 --> 49:28.726
You can't just say "love you" without taking action or changing, can you?

1136
49:30.280 --> 49:33.598
Right, we'll distribute the set-up guides to each company.

1137
49:33.598 --> 49:34.685
- Yes, sir. - Yes, sir.

1138
49:34.685 --> 49:36.784
Alright, that's all for now.

1139
49:43.343 --> 49:45.430
Alright, apart from that...

1140
49:45.430 --> 49:46.727
Second Company Commander.

1141
49:46.727 --> 49:47.992
Yes?

1142
49:47.992 --> 49:51.122
Keep one thing in mind, too.

1143
49:51.122 --> 49:53.744
I didn't ask for your opinion.

1144
49:53.744 --> 49:55.563
It was an order.

1145
49:57.036 --> 49:58.444
Yes, I understand.

1146
49:58.444 --> 50:00.931
- Chungseong! - Good job.

1147
50:01.864 --> 50:04.459
- Continue like that. - Yes, sir.

1148
50:15.804 --> 50:18.815
- Chungseong. Love you! - Yeah, love you.

1149
50:18.815 --> 50:20.866
- Hee Jeong, make a cafe. - Yes, sir?

1150
50:20.866 --> 50:22.080
W-What kind of cafe?

1151
50:22.080 --> 50:23.185
An online Daum Cafe.

1152
50:23.185 --> 50:24.815
Orders from the battalion commander.

1153
50:24.815 --> 50:28.038
Set it up, then contact the soldiers' parents

1154
50:28.038 --> 50:30.547
so they can get updates on how their sons are doing.

1155
50:30.547 --> 50:32.895
Wait, is that allowed, sir?

1156
50:32.895 --> 50:35.936
He said it's an order. A notice should've been sent through, check it.

1157
50:35.936 --> 50:37.725
I'll check now, sir.

1158
50:44.917 --> 50:47.670
- Yoon Mo. - Corporal Sung Yoon Mo.

1159
50:50.949 --> 50:52.538
Go to the internet cafe,

1160
50:52.538 --> 50:54.378
use the manual to make it, and report back.

1161
50:54.378 --> 50:55.929
[Guide to Set-up and Operate] Okay, I will.

1162
50:55.929 --> 50:57.933
[the Unit Online Cafe] Use a proper admin password this time.

1163
50:57.933 --> 51:00.924
None of that confusing 18-digit Pi nonsense like last time.

1164
51:00.924 --> 51:02.152
Yes, okay.

1165
51:02.152 --> 51:04.922
Something difficult to crack, but you won't forget.

1166
51:08.847 --> 51:10.633
Yeah, okay.

1167
51:12.416 --> 51:14.551
Why does my poop keep coming out like rabbit droppings?

1168
51:14.551 --> 51:16.504
Jeez.

1169
51:16.504 --> 51:18.733
What did you set as the password?

1170
51:19.602 --> 51:23.418
I made something difficult to crack, but I won't forget.

1171
51:23.418 --> 51:24.882
Okay, so what is it?

1172
51:24.882 --> 51:26.269
Sorry?

1173
51:26.875 --> 51:28.388
Show me.

1174
51:31.213 --> 51:32.628
Here.

1175
51:34.273 --> 51:35.592
[NHJIAB] What's this?

1176
51:35.592 --> 51:36.862
It's tricky.

1177
51:36.862 --> 51:39.425
I'm going to the restroom.

1178
51:39.425 --> 51:41.190
Wait a second.

1179
51:42.895 --> 51:44.390
"N", No.

1180
51:44.390 --> 51:47.181
"H" Hee, "J" Jeong.

1181
51:47.985 --> 51:50.720
"Is A Bast..."

1182
51:51.942 --> 51:52.956
"ion."

1183
51:52.956 --> 51:55.563
"Is a bastion."

1184
51:56.377 --> 51:58.656
You prick, come here!

1185
51:58.656 --> 52:00.510
You need a beating, come here!

1186
52:00.510 --> 52:01.622
- Get over here! - No, I...

1187
52:01.622 --> 52:03.035
Come here, you bastard, come on!

1188
52:03.035 --> 52:05.223
This prick, you, you deserve a beating!

1189
52:05.223 --> 52:06.920
- Oh, oh, wait! - Huh?

1190
52:06.920 --> 52:09.302
- Oh? - You're back, sir?

1191
52:09.302 --> 52:10.729
Are you harassing Yoon Mo right now?

1192
52:10.729 --> 52:11.832
N-No, sir.

1193
52:11.832 --> 52:12.842
You were though?

1194
52:12.842 --> 52:15.399
I was just hugging him, sir!

1195
52:15.399 --> 52:16.783
Was he really hugging you?

1196
52:16.783 --> 52:17.940
Yes, he was, sir.

1197
52:17.940 --> 52:19.375
- Yeah. - I don't think he was.

1198
52:19.375 --> 52:22.257
N-No, seriously, I was giving him a good, tight hug!

1199
52:22.257 --> 52:23.903
- Oh, Sergeant First Class Im. - Hi, sir.

1200
52:23.903 --> 52:26.111
Here you go.

1201
52:26.111 --> 52:29.262
As you go around, please take a good mix of photos of the guys

1202
52:29.262 --> 52:31.094
working and going about their day!

1203
52:31.094 --> 52:32.376
- Yes, sir! - Great.

1204
52:32.376 --> 52:34.553
Just nothing that could be classified, yeah?

1205
52:34.553 --> 52:36.462
- Got it, sir! - Great, good work!

1206
52:36.462 --> 52:37.497
Chungseong! Love you!

1207
52:37.497 --> 52:39.085
Yes, love you!

1208
52:39.085 --> 52:42.333
- Don't harass him! - No, s-seriously, I didn't!

1209
52:44.530 --> 52:47.284
Go to the internet cafe and change the password, now.

1210
52:47.284 --> 52:49.887
Yes, okay.

1211
52:49.887 --> 52:51.969
Now we're camera guys,

1212
52:51.969 --> 52:54.706
exposing the entire unit.

1213
52:54.706 --> 52:56.896
What a well-run military.

1214
52:56.896 --> 53:01.134
Platoon Sergeant, any chance you could take pictures of us too, then?

1215
53:01.134 --> 53:02.875
- Sure, of course. - A lone-wolf admin clerk vibe!

1216
53:02.875 --> 53:04.125
- Yes, yes! - Oh wow, really?

1217
53:04.125 --> 53:06.019
Let's pose, quickly!

1218
53:06.019 --> 53:07.419
Please make us look good!

1219
53:07.419 --> 53:08.693
Hey, of course!

1220
53:08.693 --> 53:12.036
- Kind of lone wolf-esque... - Yeah, yeah, cool.

1221
53:12.036 --> 53:13.402
Right.

1222
53:13.402 --> 53:15.014
Okay, taking it!

1223
53:15.014 --> 53:17.191
One, two...

1224
53:17.191 --> 53:18.955
- Three, these bastards! - Sorry, sir!

1225
53:18.955 --> 53:21.975
Are you joking? Take it yourself, damn.

1226
53:21.975 --> 53:23.823
Idiots.

1227
53:26.589 --> 53:28.914
I would speak out if it were wrong,

1228
53:28.914 --> 53:31.949
but this doesn't seem like a right-or-wrong problem.

1229
53:31.949 --> 53:34.857
I don't know what the right call is...

1230
53:34.857 --> 53:37.970
But I feel like something's going to happen.

1231
53:40.127 --> 53:42.151
Announcement from the admin office.

1232
53:42.151 --> 53:44.852
Please check today's guard duty rota.

1233
53:44.852 --> 53:46.326
- Once again, please check... - Hyeon Uk.

1234
53:46.326 --> 53:48.465
I'll go, don't worry, I'll be right back!

1235
53:48.465 --> 53:49.472
See you in a bit.

1236
53:49.472 --> 53:51.085
Thank you!

1237
53:59.902 --> 54:01.161
You did well!

1238
54:01.161 --> 54:02.367
- Corporal Park Min Seok! - Yeah?

1239
54:02.367 --> 54:04.476
You and Hyeon Uk are on 2 a.m. duty!

1240
54:04.476 --> 54:06.197
- Oh really? - Yes, sir.

1241
54:06.197 --> 54:08.328
Hyeon Uk, this is your first guard posting, right?

1242
54:08.328 --> 54:09.929
Private Kim Hyeon Uk. Yes, sir, it is!

1243
54:09.929 --> 54:11.876
- Come sit! - Yes, sir.

1244
54:11.876 --> 54:14.197
Hey, brief him well so yesterday's mess doesn't happen again.

1245
54:14.197 --> 54:17.369
I will, sir, but we're going together, so it should be fine.

1246
54:17.369 --> 54:19.236
Keep your wits about you, Min Seok.

1247
54:19.236 --> 54:21.925
I will, no need to worry!

1248
54:21.925 --> 54:24.275
Did you memorize all the passwords?

1249
54:25.845 --> 54:27.301
Cute.

1250
54:29.949 --> 54:31.708
Don't smile!

1251
54:32.778 --> 54:36.657
Goddammit, why does the First Sergeant keep calling me out for drinks?

1252
54:36.657 --> 54:40.787
As if things aren't hard enough, now I have to drink shitty booze.

1253
54:42.613 --> 54:44.756
Wait, Park Min Ju?

1254
54:44.756 --> 54:46.530
Why is she here?

1255
54:46.530 --> 54:47.629
So cool.

1256
54:47.629 --> 54:48.966
Huh?

1257
54:48.966 --> 54:50.540
What the hell.

1258
54:50.540 --> 54:52.649
Im Seong Min, damn...

1259
54:52.649 --> 54:54.386
What the hell?

1260
54:59.046 --> 55:01.680
Sergeant First Class Park Min Ju?

1261
55:01.680 --> 55:04.468
Sergeant First Class Park!

1262
55:04.468 --> 55:06.139
Chungseong!

1263
55:10.643 --> 55:13.197
I-It's me, it's Staff Sergeant Choi Il Gu!

1264
55:13.197 --> 55:14.689
"Choi Il Gu?"

1265
55:14.689 --> 55:18.623
I-I used to be Min Seok's squad leader and made staff sergeant recently...

1266
55:20.234 --> 55:21.249
Sorry.

1267
55:21.249 --> 55:23.760
- I... - My body tends to react first, so...

1268
55:23.760 --> 55:26.749
Jeez... I nearly died.

1269
55:26.749 --> 55:29.273
Any later and you would've.

1270
55:30.945 --> 55:33.974
What brings you out here though?

1271
55:33.974 --> 55:36.860
- I see... - It's not like that.

1272
55:37.698 --> 55:38.705
It's not!

1273
55:38.705 --> 55:42.976
I didn't say anything!

1274
55:42.976 --> 55:44.850
- If you have time, then... - Yes?

1275
55:44.850 --> 55:46.582
you want to die?

1276
55:47.281 --> 55:50.242
Oh my, I'm sorry.

1277
55:50.242 --> 55:52.575
Keep what you saw here today a secret.

1278
55:52.575 --> 55:54.535
Oh, yes, ma'am.

1279
55:54.535 --> 55:56.147
Right, then.

1280
55:56.147 --> 55:57.515
I'll take the bill now!

1281
55:57.515 --> 56:00.300
Would it be okay...

1282
56:00.300 --> 56:04.092
if I helped you out?

1283
56:05.571 --> 56:06.646
Really?

1284
56:06.646 --> 56:10.447
Yes, really.

1285
56:12.676 --> 56:14.480
Lights out!

1286
56:18.339 --> 56:19.539
Setting.

1287
56:19.539 --> 56:20.713
Yes, okay.

1288
56:20.713 --> 56:23.529
- Byeong Ho. - Corporal Cha Byeong Ho, confirmed.

1289
56:28.468 --> 56:30.244
What are you doing?

1290
56:32.583 --> 56:34.383
Corporal Cha Byeong Ho, blackout complete.

1291
56:34.383 --> 56:36.134
Corporal Ji Jeong Min, remote control ready.

1292
56:36.134 --> 56:37.225
- Good. - Hey!

1293
56:37.225 --> 56:39.410
The minute you hear footsteps, kill it, seriously, okay?

1294
56:39.410 --> 56:41.434
Just trust me!

1295
56:41.434 --> 56:42.977
If you pull that crap you did last time

1296
56:42.977 --> 56:45.315
and cut it at the best bit, you're dead, for real.

1297
56:45.315 --> 56:46.703
It'll be different this time!

1298
56:46.703 --> 56:47.781
Whatever, turn it on.

1299
56:47.781 --> 56:49.754
Yes, sir.

1300
56:49.754 --> 56:52.424
- I can take over! - It's okay, you do it later.

1301
56:53.099 --> 56:54.544
[1997]

1302
56:54.544 --> 56:56.235
Oh, crap!

1303
56:56.917 --> 56:58.106
Hey, you're increasing it!

1304
56:58.106 --> 57:00.135
Sorry!

1305
57:00.135 --> 57:01.855
Yeah, 3 is good, do 3!

1306
57:01.855 --> 57:03.455
[Reply 1997] Okay!

1307
57:07.744 --> 57:10.285
Hey, hey, it's on!

1308
57:10.285 --> 57:12.718
Isn't the husband getting revealed today?

1309
57:12.718 --> 57:14.346
You're right!

1310
57:16.092 --> 57:17.909
- Hyeon Uk. - Private Kim Hyeon Uk!

1311
57:17.909 --> 57:20.307
I'll let you watch the rerun this weekend.

1312
57:20.307 --> 57:23.121
- Okay, sir! - Damn, what's gonna happen?

1313
57:23.121 --> 57:25.325
Who the hell is that?

1314
57:25.325 --> 57:27.502
If I could smoke right now, this would be perfect.

1315
57:27.502 --> 57:30.926
Man, ever since you got a girlfriend, you've been chain-smoking.

1316
57:30.926 --> 57:32.532
Guys, don't get a girlfriend.

1317
57:32.532 --> 57:34.500
What a load of bullshit, honestly.

1318
57:34.500 --> 57:36.654
- Se Gye. - Private First Class Jeon Se Gye!

1319
57:36.654 --> 57:38.535
Do you know who the husband is?

1320
57:38.535 --> 57:40.543
Shall I tell you?

1321
57:40.543 --> 57:42.483
- Yeah! - Wait, what, you know?

1322
57:42.483 --> 57:43.951
I know all the actors.

1323
57:43.951 --> 57:45.545
I met them when they were filming that, too.

1324
57:45.545 --> 57:46.552
Oh, that's right!

1325
57:46.552 --> 57:50.465
Dealing with those pricks these days has made me forget who Jeon Sekai is!

1326
57:50.465 --> 57:52.176
Private First Class Jeon Sekai.

1327
57:52.176 --> 57:53.586
Whatever.

1328
57:53.586 --> 57:54.823
So, who is it?

1329
57:54.823 --> 57:56.458
I missed last week's episode too.

1330
57:56.458 --> 57:58.503
I really need to watch the finale until the very end today.

1331
57:58.503 --> 58:00.196
- Lalalala... - It's Yoon Jae for sure!

1332
58:00.196 --> 58:01.971
I think it's Yoon Jae's brother.

1333
58:01.971 --> 58:04.188
It could even be Bang Seong Jae.

1334
58:04.188 --> 58:07.187
No way, it's definitely one of the brothers!

1335
58:07.187 --> 58:09.128
Should I...

1336
58:09.128 --> 58:11.084
- really tell you? - Yes!

1337
58:11.084 --> 58:12.725
The...

1338
58:12.725 --> 58:13.764
husband is...

1339
58:13.764 --> 58:16.178
Hey! I'm going to watch it, so no spoilers!

1340
58:16.178 --> 58:17.774
This is all I've been waiting for.

1341
58:17.774 --> 58:20.069
This bastard always ruins the mood, I swear, damn.

1342
58:20.069 --> 58:21.679
What?

1343
58:31.431 --> 58:33.518
Hey, look at In Guk go.

1344
58:33.518 --> 58:35.964
Woah, so exciting!

1345
58:35.964 --> 58:38.617
What will we watch once this is over?

1346
58:38.617 --> 58:40.665
The husband's being revealed soon!

1347
58:45.223 --> 58:47.511
Guys, lie down, lie down!

1348
58:59.199 --> 59:00.969
[Barracks No.3]

1349
59:08.875 --> 59:11.228
Everyone's fast asleep.

1350
59:11.228 --> 59:12.828
Good.

1351
59:21.266 --> 59:22.665
Ji Jeong Min, nice!

1352
59:22.665 --> 59:24.319
Corporal Ji Jeong Min!

1353
59:24.319 --> 59:26.138
Thank you!

1354
59:26.897 --> 59:28.669
How did you know it was the company commander?

1355
59:28.669 --> 59:30.306
Are you stepping up as the ace now?

1356
59:30.306 --> 59:32.140
These damn amateurs!

1357
59:32.140 --> 59:34.803
It's all in the footsteps!

1358
59:34.803 --> 59:37.549
The night watch guards scamper around quickly.

1359
59:37.549 --> 59:41.250
But the officers are like "boom, boom, boom!"

1360
59:41.250 --> 59:43.221
Like they're scoping as they walk!

1361
59:43.221 --> 59:45.197
Now that's seniority...

1362
59:47.075 --> 59:49.099
Was that just my imagination?

1363
59:49.099 --> 59:51.386
I swear you guys were awake.

1364
59:52.339 --> 59:55.727
Looks like you're all asleep, though?

1365
59:55.727 --> 59:57.723
That's so strange.

1366
59:57.723 --> 01:00:01.202
The top feels all warm, like a TV that's just been turned off.

1367
01:00:01.202 --> 01:00:03.462
It's weird, right, Jeong Min?

1368
01:00:03.462 --> 01:00:06.411
C-Corporal Ji Jeong Min!

1369
01:00:08.799 --> 01:00:10.479
Sorry, sir.

1370
01:00:10.479 --> 01:00:11.868
Were you watching "Reply 1997?"

1371
01:00:11.868 --> 01:00:13.363
Yes, I was.

1372
01:00:13.363 --> 01:00:15.911
Okay, I like that one too, so I understand!

1373
01:00:15.911 --> 01:00:17.162
Thank you, sir!

1374
01:00:17.162 --> 01:00:18.717
- Don't watch it! - Yes, sir.

1375
01:00:18.717 --> 01:00:19.925
Stop watching, starting now!

1376
01:00:19.925 --> 01:00:21.426
- Yes, sir! - Seriously, don't!

1377
01:00:21.426 --> 01:00:22.452
I won't, sir!

1378
01:00:22.452 --> 01:00:24.672
- Goodnight! - Yeah.

1379
01:00:25.822 --> 01:00:27.628
Man, it never goes right.

1380
01:00:27.628 --> 01:00:28.887
I'm so sorry.

1381
01:00:28.887 --> 01:00:30.752
- Right, set it up again. - Okay, on it.

1382
01:00:30.752 --> 01:00:31.840
I'll do it this time!

1383
01:00:31.840 --> 01:00:33.731
Okay, World Jeon, you do it!

1384
01:00:35.008 --> 01:00:36.907
- Do it well! - Okay!

1385
01:00:37.780 --> 01:00:40.956
Hey, I bet 10,000 won of frozen snacks that it's Yoon Jae's brother!

1386
01:00:40.956 --> 01:00:43.667
I bet it's not, and I'll get snacks from PX!

1387
01:00:43.667 --> 01:00:45.050
- PX it is, then! - PX bread!

1388
01:00:45.050 --> 01:00:48.282
Hey, be quiet, guys. The volume's at 3 so it's hard to hear!

1389
01:00:49.593 --> 01:00:50.895
Ugh, I'm envious.

1390
01:00:50.895 --> 01:00:53.775
I wonder if my Su Ah's watching this too.

1391
01:00:53.775 --> 01:00:56.209
I want to get married, too, damn.

1392
01:00:57.367 --> 01:00:59.018
He's gonna come out now!

1393
01:00:59.018 --> 01:01:00.639
There, there!

1394
01:01:02.579 --> 01:01:04.088
That scared me.

1395
01:01:06.350 --> 01:01:09.810
I'm today's DJ, Baek Ho!

1396
01:01:09.810 --> 01:01:13.442
You're all probably dying to know who the husband is right now.

1397
01:01:13.442 --> 01:01:16.284
Everyone knows I'm not that strict,

1398
01:01:16.284 --> 01:01:18.219
so why are you all sneaking around?

1399
01:01:18.219 --> 01:01:22.421
If the squad leaders had just come and asked, I would've let you watch it!

1400
01:01:22.421 --> 01:01:26.395
No, don't come over now, it's lights out!

1401
01:01:26.395 --> 01:01:28.567
You guys didn't tell me,

1402
01:01:28.567 --> 01:01:31.077
but I'll tell you guys.

1403
01:01:31.077 --> 01:01:33.402
- Tell us what? - What?

1404
01:01:33.402 --> 01:01:34.812
Oh wait, no, no!

1405
01:01:34.812 --> 01:01:37.533
- No... - No, I don't want to know!

1406
01:01:40.916 --> 01:01:42.024
He's coming.

1407
01:01:42.024 --> 01:01:43.093
Oh?

1408
01:01:43.093 --> 01:01:45.308
Spit it out, man, run, run!

1409
01:01:48.823 --> 01:01:50.075
You say it first!

1410
01:01:50.075 --> 01:01:52.566
Spit it out, come on, quickly!

1411
01:01:53.752 --> 01:01:55.253
- No, no, no! - Quickly!

1412
01:01:55.253 --> 01:01:56.755
Who is it?

1413
01:01:58.257 --> 01:02:00.941
The husband's Yoon Yoon Jae! That's all, good night!

1414
01:02:00.941 --> 01:02:02.010
What!

1415
01:02:02.010 --> 01:02:03.806
- No way! - That's not true, right?

1416
01:02:03.806 --> 01:02:06.430
N-No way, no, it's not.

1417
01:02:08.009 --> 01:02:09.885
I'm her husband.

1418
01:02:15.739 --> 01:02:17.349
I can't believe it. It's a joke!

1419
01:02:17.349 --> 01:02:19.694
It's Yoon Jae?

1420
01:02:19.694 --> 01:02:22.858
- Why did he do that, seriously! - Commander Cho, why!

1421
01:02:22.858 --> 01:02:24.052
This fucking sucks.

1422
01:02:24.052 --> 01:02:26.459
- Let's sleep now. - Good night.

1423
01:02:26.459 --> 01:02:27.917
Seriously, man!

1424
01:02:27.917 --> 01:02:30.228
He's so mean, honestly!

1425
01:02:30.228 --> 01:02:31.762
Yoon Yoon Jae.

1426
01:02:31.762 --> 01:02:33.272
Yoon Yoon Jae.

1427
01:02:33.272 --> 01:02:36.111
I really liked the company commander...

1428
01:02:36.111 --> 01:02:37.430
Not anymore, though.

1429
01:02:37.430 --> 01:02:40.276
Seriously, he's too harsh!

1430
01:02:40.276 --> 01:02:43.176
- Turn the TV off. - Yes, sir.

1431
01:02:46.535 --> 01:02:48.771
- Where are you going? - I'm going to get the gun store key.

1432
01:02:48.771 --> 01:02:49.926
Stop him. He's being for real.

1433
01:02:49.926 --> 01:02:51.353
Huh? You can't!

1434
01:02:51.353 --> 01:02:53.544
N-No, you can't!

1435
01:02:53.544 --> 01:02:55.338
He said Yoon Yoon Jae.

1436
01:02:55.338 --> 01:02:56.815
Give me a hug.

1437
01:02:56.815 --> 01:02:59.182
Private First Class Jeon Se Gye.

1438
01:03:01.059 --> 01:03:02.521
Cozy.

1439
01:03:03.912 --> 01:03:06.743
That's entertaining, too!

1440
01:03:13.239 --> 01:03:14.776
Oh my.

1441
01:03:15.991 --> 01:03:18.355
- Company Commander! - What?

1442
01:03:18.355 --> 01:03:19.875
Seriously!

1443
01:03:19.875 --> 01:03:21.701
Isn't that too cruel?

1444
01:03:21.701 --> 01:03:23.295
Do you know what my nickname is?

1445
01:03:23.295 --> 01:03:24.320
I don't, sir!

1446
01:03:24.320 --> 01:03:26.095
"Spoiler Mario!"

1447
01:03:26.095 --> 01:03:27.560
"Spoiler Mario..."

1448
01:03:27.560 --> 01:03:30.697
But how did you know who the husband was?

1449
01:03:30.697 --> 01:03:33.047
If you saw last week's episode, it's obvious!

1450
01:03:33.047 --> 01:03:34.129
That was fun!

1451
01:03:34.129 --> 01:03:35.797
For God's sake!

1452
01:03:35.797 --> 01:03:37.342
Dong Woo.

1453
01:03:37.342 --> 01:03:38.655
Corporal Kim Dong Woo!

1454
01:03:38.655 --> 01:03:40.234
Want some ramen?

1455
01:03:40.234 --> 01:03:42.550
- Yes, sir! - Great!

1456
01:03:49.931 --> 01:03:54.012
Now I can really... see the end.

1457
01:03:59.515 --> 01:04:01.279
But there's nothing you can do as a private.

1458
01:04:01.279 --> 01:04:03.344
It was always like that for me as a private.

1459
01:04:03.344 --> 01:04:05.172
I was scolded every day.

1460
01:04:05.172 --> 01:04:09.336
But you're doing well, so honestly there's nothing to worry about.

1461
01:04:09.336 --> 01:04:13.489
When you get to corporal, it's honestly so great.

1462
01:04:13.489 --> 01:04:15.680
They always say time's so slow to pass,

1463
01:04:15.680 --> 01:04:18.241
but it does eventually.

1464
01:04:19.228 --> 01:04:22.265
Oh, it's already time!

1465
01:04:22.265 --> 01:04:24.823
Have I been talking too much about myself?

1466
01:04:24.823 --> 01:04:26.752
No, sir!

1467
01:04:26.752 --> 01:04:29.221
- It was interesting! - Really?

1468
01:04:32.719 --> 01:04:35.619
How are you settling in?

1469
01:04:35.619 --> 01:04:39.003
Thanks to you, it's been easier.

1470
01:04:39.003 --> 01:04:41.192
Oh, really? Thanks!

1471
01:04:44.297 --> 01:04:47.266
What a strange coincidence, right?

1472
01:04:48.632 --> 01:04:50.559
Yes, that's right.

1473
01:04:50.559 --> 01:04:52.814
Really, when I first saw you,

1474
01:04:52.814 --> 01:04:54.828
I thought, "This is fate."

1475
01:04:54.828 --> 01:04:56.472
Right?

1476
01:04:56.472 --> 01:04:58.619
I really thought we'd never cross paths again

1477
01:04:58.619 --> 01:05:00.917
after we left training camp!

1478
01:05:00.917 --> 01:05:02.891
It's so strange!

1479
01:05:05.902 --> 01:05:07.539
Someone's coming.

1480
01:05:07.539 --> 01:05:10.629
It's Corporal Kim Dong Woo coming to change shifts.

1481
01:05:15.697 --> 01:05:17.873
- Hyeon Uk. - Private Hyeon Uk.

1482
01:05:17.873 --> 01:05:19.861
How was it, manageable?

1483
01:05:19.861 --> 01:05:21.558
- Yes, sir. - Wow.

1484
01:05:21.558 --> 01:05:24.829
Once you've done it a few times, you'll be sick of it!

1485
01:05:25.640 --> 01:05:28.270
Did Park Min Seok just blabber on about himself?

1486
01:05:28.270 --> 01:05:29.469
No, sir!

1487
01:05:29.469 --> 01:05:31.559
Oh, well, I kind of did.

1488
01:05:31.559 --> 01:05:33.407
But still, only about fun stuff!

1489
01:05:33.407 --> 01:05:34.853
Really, like what?

1490
01:05:34.853 --> 01:05:37.052
About all the ups and downs in my life.

1491
01:05:37.052 --> 01:05:38.547
And, well,

1492
01:05:38.547 --> 01:05:40.609
talking about girls who confessed to me, stuff like that.

1493
01:05:40.609 --> 01:05:41.746
You sure those weren't rejections?

1494
01:05:41.746 --> 01:05:43.474
I've never been rejected before!

1495
01:05:43.474 --> 01:05:45.417
- Really? - Yeah, I'm super popular!

1496
01:05:45.417 --> 01:05:46.500
The short hair helps!

1497
01:05:46.500 --> 01:05:48.775
I was no joke when my hair was long.

1498
01:05:48.775 --> 01:05:50.213
Always keep your finger off the trigger.

1499
01:05:50.213 --> 01:05:51.679
Understood, sir.

1500
01:05:55.035 --> 01:05:56.674
Hyeon Uk, you tried it at training camp, right?

1501
01:05:56.674 --> 01:05:57.731
Yes, sir.

1502
01:05:57.731 --> 01:05:59.093
If you're not sure, just copy Min Seok.

1503
01:05:59.093 --> 01:06:00.246
Yes, understood.

1504
01:06:00.246 --> 01:06:02.762
- Present arms. - Presenting.

1505
01:06:02.762 --> 01:06:05.355
- Remove magazine. - Removing.

1506
01:06:05.355 --> 01:06:06.885
Corporal Park Min Seok, no issues.

1507
01:06:06.885 --> 01:06:09.060
Private Kim Hyeon Uk, no issues.

1508
01:06:09.060 --> 01:06:10.660
Private Kim Hyeon Uk.

1509
01:06:11.348 --> 01:06:15.511
- Cycle the bolt two or three times. - Cycling the bolt two or three times.

1510
01:06:15.511 --> 01:06:18.317
- Check the chamber. - Checking the chamber. Chamber is clear.

1511
01:06:18.317 --> 01:06:21.564
- Shoulder arms. - Shoulder arms.

1512
01:06:21.564 --> 01:06:23.412
- Selector to semi. - Selector to semi.

1513
01:06:23.412 --> 01:06:24.864
- Fire. - Firing.

1514
01:06:24.864 --> 01:06:26.289
Trigger pull, all clear.

1515
01:06:26.289 --> 01:06:27.746
Fire.

1516
01:06:32.478 --> 01:06:34.604
- What was that? - What?

1517
01:06:36.276 --> 01:06:38.113
Was that a gunshot?

1518
01:06:39.715 --> 01:06:41.287
Assistant Platoon Leader! We have a problem!

1519
01:06:41.287 --> 01:06:43.114
- What happened? - Well... outside...

1520
01:06:43.114 --> 01:06:44.759
Speak up, you punk. What happened?

1521
01:06:44.759 --> 01:06:47.625
I was checking the gun, then...
